1
00:00:09,420 --> 00:02:09,419
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com

2
00:02:10,240 --> 00:02:13,940
Episode 82

3
00:02:30,340 --> 00:02:31,720
Gunduz Bey!

4
00:02:32,580 --> 00:02:34,160
Osman Bey.

5
00:02:35,180 --> 00:02:36,490
Come here.

6
00:02:39,940 --> 00:02:41,960
Come here, Gunduz Bey.

7
00:02:46,410 --> 00:02:47,710
I don't want....

8
00:02:48,900 --> 00:02:51,730
...my brothers and alps blood to shed.

9
00:03:11,760 --> 00:03:13,780
You take alps with you...

10
00:03:15,440 --> 00:03:18,230
...and let the cruels destroy Turks!

11
00:03:21,220 --> 00:03:22,990
They are not to blame!

12
00:03:24,080 --> 00:03:30,880
You deceive them with Vizier and Geyhatu.

13
00:03:48,460 --> 00:03:55,500
You have witnessed throughout your life
what my sword did to the cruels.

14
00:03:59,150 --> 00:04:01,730
Now that you are one of the cruels now...

15
00:04:03,560 --> 00:04:05,100
Then...

16
00:04:11,140 --> 00:04:13,500
You shall get to know
the justice of my sword.

17
00:04:18,089 --> 00:04:20,230
Come on, Gunduz Bey.

18
00:04:24,360 --> 00:04:27,910
Since you consider me an enemy...

19
00:04:31,520 --> 00:04:35,020
Then, I won't back down either, brother.

20
00:04:36,810 --> 00:04:39,510
After all the betrayals you've done...

21
00:04:40,620 --> 00:04:44,530
After all that injustice,
do you still call me "brother"?

22
00:04:47,460 --> 00:04:48,930
Which brothers?

23
00:04:51,720 --> 00:04:56,020
From now on I'm not your brother!

24
00:04:56,630 --> 00:04:58,950
I wouldn't end my brother!

25
00:05:08,160 --> 00:05:10,630
Because of the betrayals you committed....

26
00:05:13,280 --> 00:05:16,240
Your blood is halal to me!

27
00:05:20,480 --> 00:05:25,260
You are a son who betrayed his ancestors.

28
00:05:25,860 --> 00:05:30,870
You are an older brother who left
his younger brother among traitors!

29
00:05:32,000 --> 00:05:37,000
You are a Bey who
has turned his back on his country

30
00:05:42,780 --> 00:05:48,560
You will leave this world without a brother...

31
00:05:49,260 --> 00:05:51,040
a tradition...

32
00:05:52,260 --> 00:05:54,250
and a homeland!

33
00:05:59,970 --> 00:06:01,140
Come here.

34
00:06:23,370 --> 00:06:25,660
"Two days ago"

35
00:06:32,340 --> 00:06:35,950
You really want to kill me, don't you,
Osman Bey?

36
00:06:37,920 --> 00:06:40,010
I can tell it from my own experiences.

37
00:06:41,770 --> 00:06:43,370
Believe me.

38
00:06:43,390 --> 00:06:48,950
There is nothing on this earth
more beautiful than your disappearance.

39
00:06:58,580 --> 00:07:00,870
For the great enemy...

40
00:07:03,880 --> 00:07:05,450
We will ally.

41
00:07:08,700 --> 00:07:10,260
Alliance?

42
00:07:13,970 --> 00:07:15,900
Alliance?

43
00:07:19,460 --> 00:07:23,330
I don't need to ally with anyone.

44
00:07:23,960 --> 00:07:25,740
I am Aya Nikola.

45
00:07:29,160 --> 00:07:33,950
Because the sun is behind you,
you think your shadow is too big

46
00:07:43,910 --> 00:07:47,100
If you don't need anyone...

47
00:07:48,030 --> 00:07:50,420
Why do gather the Lords?

48
00:07:52,950 --> 00:07:55,260
How do you know this?

49
00:07:56,220 --> 00:07:58,040
So, it's not just me.

50
00:07:58,540 --> 00:08:00,670
Geyhatu knows it too.

51
00:08:01,320 --> 00:08:04,320
And he knows that you're
spinning games behind him!

52
00:08:04,620 --> 00:08:07,940
For this reason,
he sent his soldiers to behead you.

53
00:08:12,700 --> 00:08:18,870
Not only you,
but if all the Lords gathered...

54
00:08:19,620 --> 00:08:26,800
You can't do anything in front of the 20,000
Mongol soldiers Arghun Khan sent to Geyhatu.

55
00:08:27,260 --> 00:08:28,300
...20

56
00:08:32,470 --> 00:08:33,780
20

57
00:08:37,630 --> 00:08:39,700
20,000?

58
00:08:46,180 --> 00:08:47,460
20,000?

59
00:08:49,960 --> 00:08:51,710
Follow me.

60
00:08:58,360 --> 00:09:02,400
Argun Khan's soldiers are coming.

61
00:09:03,070 --> 00:09:06,170
They will put down the rebellion
of the Turks.

62
00:09:06,860 --> 00:09:11,280
Argun Khan is going straight east.

63
00:09:12,530 --> 00:09:17,160
His army will be under my command.

64
00:09:19,540 --> 00:09:23,860
I will destroy Argun Khan.

65
00:09:25,700 --> 00:09:28,610
His throne will be mine.

66
00:09:29,050 --> 00:09:34,010
And the Seljuk state will also
be within my palm!

67
00:09:36,150 --> 00:09:40,060
Sultan Mesut is at the door of death.

68
00:09:40,400 --> 00:09:44,560
But even when he is like this,
he is still a strong man

69
00:09:45,270 --> 00:09:47,840
You underestimate him too much.

70
00:09:48,610 --> 00:09:51,920
He will do everything to stop you.

71
00:09:51,920 --> 00:09:55,770
I am greater than death, Alam Shah.

72
00:09:56,800 --> 00:09:59,980
Mesut can't do anything.

73
00:10:00,530 --> 00:10:04,280
His youngest son will become the sultan.

74
00:10:04,950 --> 00:10:08,410
And you will become his viceroy(yabgu).

75
00:10:09,160 --> 00:10:12,240
The judgment will be yours

76
00:10:16,550 --> 00:10:17,760
But first...

77
00:10:19,110 --> 00:10:21,630
Nikola.

78
00:10:22,180 --> 00:10:25,180
Nicola won't be able to
achieve what he hopes.

79
00:10:25,760 --> 00:10:31,080
If Nikola had gathered the Lords for war
in order to fulfill his hopes...

80
00:10:31,120 --> 00:10:33,930
This will make us lose time.

81
00:10:34,230 --> 00:10:38,250
Our time is precious, Alam Shah.

82
00:10:45,320 --> 00:10:48,580
Didn't you kill Nikola?

83
00:10:52,470 --> 00:10:53,790
Talk!

84
00:10:54,280 --> 00:10:55,820
Talk!

85
00:10:56,980 --> 00:11:00,140
I was going to bring Nikola's head to you.

86
00:11:00,530 --> 00:11:02,140
But...

87
00:11:03,090 --> 00:11:05,560
Osman showed up.

88
00:11:07,960 --> 00:11:10,020
Nikola was supposed to die!

89
00:11:10,350 --> 00:11:13,560
What was Osman doing there?

90
00:11:15,340 --> 00:11:17,870
Mingiyan!

91
00:11:23,370 --> 00:11:24,960
Gunduz Bey has come.

92
00:11:25,050 --> 00:11:26,400
Let him!

93
00:11:27,020 --> 00:11:28,360
Get out!

94
00:11:41,560 --> 00:11:44,260
20,000 soldiers are on their way.

95
00:11:46,120 --> 00:11:49,160
No one will be able to stop us.

96
00:11:52,280 --> 00:11:55,590
We'll conquer Inegol first.

97
00:11:55,870 --> 00:12:00,240
Then we will put down the rebellion in
Turkish lands.

98
00:12:05,210 --> 00:12:06,720
20,000?

99
00:12:07,840 --> 00:12:09,140
This will be a massacre.

100
00:12:09,570 --> 00:12:14,760
The end of the rebels must
be a massacre, Gündüz.

101
00:12:16,740 --> 00:12:19,640
You will see and take a lesson out of it.

102
00:12:24,710 --> 00:12:29,600
You will come with your alps,
as you promised, Gündüz

103
00:12:30,910 --> 00:12:34,900
You will fight on our side.

104
00:12:40,980 --> 00:12:46,430
Now the Mongols will attack
us like a torrent!

105
00:12:47,480 --> 00:12:51,100
It's such a torrent that...

106
00:12:52,470 --> 00:12:55,840
it will ruin every nation!

107
00:12:57,210 --> 00:13:01,990
He's knocking on our door now.

108
00:13:03,320 --> 00:13:05,770
He knocked on your door, Osman Bey.

109
00:13:06,180 --> 00:13:10,100
If he ends me, he will come for you soon.

110
00:13:12,330 --> 00:13:14,780
Turks, Romans...

111
00:13:15,650 --> 00:13:17,180
ّSeljuqs...

112
00:13:17,870 --> 00:13:19,340
Rome.

113
00:13:20,940 --> 00:13:23,440
We are all People of the Book.

114
00:13:25,580 --> 00:13:27,980
We must unite against these oppressors.

115
00:13:27,980 --> 00:13:30,650
Osman Bey, Osman Bey!

116
00:13:30,780 --> 00:13:34,980
You're smart and brave, okay.

117
00:13:35,340 --> 00:13:38,600
But you don't even have a throne!

118
00:13:38,600 --> 00:13:42,780
You are telling me about
confronting 20,000 Mongol soldiers!

119
00:13:44,550 --> 00:13:46,780
I am the Bey, son of the Bey.

120
00:13:47,400 --> 00:13:49,980
I don't need to prove my Beyship.

121
00:13:50,710 --> 00:13:52,290
However...

122
00:13:53,980 --> 00:13:56,620
If you don't listen to what I say...

123
00:13:57,910 --> 00:14:00,890
You won't even have a castle to
put your head in...

124
00:14:01,200 --> 00:14:04,410
These lands and Ingol...

125
00:14:05,920 --> 00:14:07,750
It's all mine.

126
00:14:08,420 --> 00:14:13,860
Neither you nor Geyhatu
can take it from me.

127
00:14:16,580 --> 00:14:18,600
Mongols won't take it from you.

128
00:14:19,740 --> 00:14:22,670
Rather, they destroy and crush.

129
00:14:24,400 --> 00:14:28,280
Samarkand, Baghdad.

130
00:14:28,520 --> 00:14:29,760
Bukhara.

131
00:14:30,300 --> 00:14:31,440
Merv.

132
00:14:32,540 --> 00:14:34,520
And many more.

133
00:14:36,710 --> 00:14:38,980
Were they weaker than Ingeol?

134
00:14:42,300 --> 00:14:44,630
Take a lesson out of this.

135
00:14:45,820 --> 00:14:49,990
...not just Inegol...

136
00:14:53,670 --> 00:14:57,000
If we do not unite against the cruels...

137
00:14:59,220 --> 00:15:02,500
The end of Constantinople
will also be the same.

138
00:15:05,050 --> 00:15:07,860
Why did I gather all the Lords?

139
00:15:11,560 --> 00:15:12,940
For war.

140
00:15:14,690 --> 00:15:18,130
I don't need you to defeat Geyhatu.

141
00:15:18,700 --> 00:15:22,900
I don't have any warrior who hasn't fought
Mongols before.

142
00:15:24,670 --> 00:15:28,720
I know strength and weakness of Mongols
very well.

143
00:15:30,410 --> 00:15:34,440
Oghuz's archers are needed
against Mongol's cavalry!

144
00:15:34,980 --> 00:15:43,504
We'll unite so we don't miss our
chance to kill each other.

145
00:15:43,598 --> 00:15:44,961
Is that it?

146
00:15:49,230 --> 00:15:50,550
Okay Osman Bey.

147
00:15:52,730 --> 00:15:55,300
Let's say I agreed.

148
00:15:56,240 --> 00:15:57,610
Let's assume that.

149
00:15:59,110 --> 00:16:00,830
What do you want from me?

150
00:16:09,640 --> 00:16:12,760
You will take me to
Emperor Andronikos.

151
00:16:16,540 --> 00:16:17,690
Osman Bey.

152
00:16:18,710 --> 00:16:23,480
You are the one who said Geyhatu knocks
on our door with 20,000 of his soldiers

153
00:16:23,480 --> 00:16:27,140
These lands will be lost
until we return from Constantinople!

154
00:16:27,680 --> 00:16:31,180
It is not us, but the emperor
will come to us.

155
00:16:33,300 --> 00:16:34,450
How?

156
00:16:37,480 --> 00:16:39,440
The Emperor is coming to Iznik.

157
00:16:41,620 --> 00:16:43,950
And you and I will go to him.

158
00:16:49,360 --> 00:16:51,040
Let everything aside...

159
00:16:52,690 --> 00:16:54,510
How do you know about this?

160
00:16:56,090 --> 00:16:58,540
We certainly know the broken branches
of great trees...

161
00:16:59,540 --> 00:17:04,680
and the future of underripe fruits.

162
00:17:06,800 --> 00:17:08,000
So...

163
00:17:09,500 --> 00:17:11,579
This is our secret :)

164
00:17:17,640 --> 00:17:21,118
Will you also include the Emperor
in the alliance?

165
00:17:21,950 --> 00:17:25,700
I'll make a non-aggression pact
with the emperor.

166
00:17:26,240 --> 00:17:31,050
The ones who leave a mountain behind do not
lose time by checking their back.

167
00:17:32,380 --> 00:17:36,000
Cengiz Khan had conquered the west
before he went for China.

168
00:17:36,560 --> 00:17:37,560
How nice.

169
00:17:38,290 --> 00:17:41,890
Do you take the men we are fighting
as an example for yourself, Osman Bey?

170
00:17:41,970 --> 00:17:43,250
No.

171
00:17:44,010 --> 00:17:46,820
I take minds as guide.

172
00:17:47,660 --> 00:17:50,960
I don't see if wisdom comes
from a friend or an enemy.

173
00:17:55,570 --> 00:17:56,810
Now...

174
00:17:57,630 --> 00:17:59,780
You will come with me to Iznik.

175
00:18:02,970 --> 00:18:04,890
I'll explain this to your emperor too.

176
00:18:06,520 --> 00:18:08,240
He will know as well...

177
00:18:09,150 --> 00:18:13,530
That if the East falls, the West will also fall.

178
00:18:20,510 --> 00:18:24,560
As long as there will be an agreement,
I mean, if it is done...

179
00:18:25,700 --> 00:18:29,340
I will have some conditions too.

180
00:18:30,080 --> 00:18:31,420
Think about your conditions.

181
00:18:33,210 --> 00:18:34,940
Tell me about them before night.

182
00:18:37,770 --> 00:18:40,110
Alps! Let's go.

183
00:18:41,010 --> 00:18:44,050
20,000 soldiers?

184
00:18:59,185 --> 00:19:03,265
Konur, my lion Konur,
Thank Allah you are alive.

185
00:19:03,975 --> 00:19:08,345
I will not die before I make him pay for
what he did to you, Vizier.

186
00:19:09,505 --> 00:19:12,115
You are wounded, did Osman do this?

187
00:19:46,065 --> 00:19:47,705
Go to the infirmary quickly.

188
00:19:47,925 --> 00:19:50,155
We'll talk about what needs
to be done later.

189
00:19:50,795 --> 00:19:52,315
Your order, Vizier.

190
00:20:00,665 --> 00:20:03,705
Celali, notify the commanders.

191
00:20:04,195 --> 00:20:06,015
They shall prepare.

192
00:20:06,255 --> 00:20:09,345
When Geyhatu commands,
we will unite with the alps of Gunduz.

193
00:20:09,345 --> 00:20:12,125
And we march to the rebellious tribes.

194
00:20:13,245 --> 00:20:14,915
Right away, Hadrat Vizier.

195
00:20:21,905 --> 00:20:25,875
-Peace be upon you
-Peace be upon you, Osman Bey.

196
00:20:26,885 --> 00:20:30,225
-Where are you headed?
-To the red apple

197
00:20:30,665 --> 00:20:33,745
- What's the point?
- Shahada!

198
00:20:34,325 --> 00:20:38,605
- For what?
- For homeland.

199
00:20:38,705 --> 00:20:42,725
- Where is homeland?
- The whole world.

200
00:20:43,055 --> 00:20:44,635
The world shall become your home.

201
00:20:46,055 --> 00:20:47,375
Welcome, Osman Bey.

202
00:20:49,615 --> 00:20:51,165
Thank you.

203
00:21:04,435 --> 00:21:08,815
Soldiers of Arghun Khan
are about to enter our lands

204
00:21:10,695 --> 00:21:11,805
Have you made your preparations?

205
00:21:12,925 --> 00:21:16,915
Did you get the Lords on your side?

206
00:21:19,075 --> 00:21:21,055
We are always on the alert

207
00:21:22,415 --> 00:21:26,675
As I told you, all the Lords
are on my side.

208
00:21:28,315 --> 00:21:32,655
These lands will become a tomb
for Arghun Khan's soldiers!

209
00:21:33,685 --> 00:21:35,835
What about the rebellious tribes?

210
00:21:36,965 --> 00:21:39,015
Let's say you have exhausted the
vanguard units

211
00:21:39,555 --> 00:21:40,925
What about the rest?

212
00:21:40,955 --> 00:21:43,135
Those who rebel will stand with us.

213
00:21:43,585 --> 00:21:45,995
We will fuel the fire of disobedience with them!

214
00:21:47,135 --> 00:21:53,915
We will encourage those who cannot raise their
heads and see the strength in themselves.

215
00:21:57,455 --> 00:22:01,695
If we burn, we burn together, and if rise,
we rise together.

216
00:22:15,525 --> 00:22:18,255
One of the units of the vanguard of Mongols
has set out on the way.

217
00:22:18,635 --> 00:22:21,155
They are coming from the direction
of Turna valley.

218
00:22:24,275 --> 00:22:25,825
Eyvallah (thank you).

219
00:22:26,885 --> 00:22:28,615
May your path be open, Osman Bey.

220
00:22:30,195 --> 00:22:31,705
Thank you.

221
00:22:57,265 --> 00:22:59,395
What are you saying my daughter?

222
00:22:59,395 --> 00:23:01,615
Yes, mother Selcan, I am pregnant.

223
00:23:03,445 --> 00:23:06,405
Yes mother,
you will have another grandchild!

224
00:23:06,675 --> 00:23:08,535
May Allah forgive your
baby's parents, Mari.

225
00:23:08,645 --> 00:23:10,395
Turgut Bey will be very pleased.

226
00:23:10,965 --> 00:23:13,755
May his/her life be long and blessings
be wide, Inshallah.

227
00:23:14,365 --> 00:23:16,505
Praise be to my pretty daughter.

228
00:23:17,625 --> 00:23:18,745
Can I come in?

229
00:23:19,825 --> 00:23:21,205
Come, Boran.

230
00:23:25,835 --> 00:23:28,675
- Peace be upon you.
- Peace be upon you

231
00:23:29,295 --> 00:23:31,805
Praise be, mother!
You are standing on your feet!

232
00:23:32,205 --> 00:23:33,685
Thank Allah very much, my son.

233
00:23:33,925 --> 00:23:36,335
My daughter Mari
gave me such news that...

234
00:23:36,835 --> 00:23:40,085
...I can cross the whole tribe
without a break, I swear to Allah

235
00:23:42,735 --> 00:23:44,685
Where are you coming from?

236
00:23:45,465 --> 00:23:47,015
From Osman Bey.

237
00:23:48,185 --> 00:23:50,125
Tell Osman quickly.

238
00:23:50,385 --> 00:23:52,315
Tell him to send Turgut Bey back
to the tribe.

239
00:23:53,505 --> 00:23:56,815
My daughter Mari
has good news to tell him.

240
00:24:00,145 --> 00:24:01,605
Your order, mother.

241
00:24:05,495 --> 00:24:07,585
And Osman Bey has also sent news.

242
00:24:07,695 --> 00:24:15,225
My Beys says that this Julia
never stops chasing after us

243
00:24:18,055 --> 00:24:20,115
Now is the time for revenge.

244
00:24:23,425 --> 00:24:24,985
It's time, Boran.

245
00:24:26,065 --> 00:24:30,675
My Gonca, Alps, and she
shed my mother's blood.

246
00:24:32,305 --> 00:24:35,345
Every breath she breathes
is a shame on us.

247
00:24:37,245 --> 00:24:39,275
Osman Bey says it too.

248
00:24:39,445 --> 00:24:41,795
This bloodless can't stop
watching the tribe.

249
00:24:42,755 --> 00:24:44,715
She will attack at the first opportunity

250
00:24:45,485 --> 00:24:49,735
He told us to get into action
before her and cut her breath.

251
00:24:51,875 --> 00:24:55,275
It's the Bey's command,
Killing her is an obligation now.

252
00:24:56,815 --> 00:25:00,615
Osman Bey knows everything,
even though he is away from his tribe.

253
00:25:00,765 --> 00:25:04,685
The hand of Osman Bey
is always above his tribe, my daughter.

254
00:25:05,265 --> 00:25:07,375
This is what a Bey looks like.

255
00:25:08,145 --> 00:25:10,575
Allah bless my valiant.

256
00:25:11,885 --> 00:25:13,655
Now listen to me carefully.

257
00:25:27,325 --> 00:25:29,845
Now that we are united...

258
00:25:30,655 --> 00:25:32,665
You need training.

259
00:25:41,965 --> 00:25:43,485
Praise be!

260
00:25:45,445 --> 00:25:46,815
Kumral!

261
00:25:47,385 --> 00:25:49,715
I've never missed you, you know?

262
00:25:49,715 --> 00:25:52,595
I entered the cave and did not
stop beating swords.

263
00:25:53,165 --> 00:25:56,305
My hands are tired, but
my head has rested.

264
00:25:58,525 --> 00:26:01,025
Good, never miss me.

265
00:26:01,855 --> 00:26:04,395
I have a new brother for myself.

266
00:26:10,315 --> 00:26:11,645
Yes.

267
00:26:11,865 --> 00:26:14,925
We are in our brother's place...

268
00:26:16,765 --> 00:26:18,825
But who is he and what does he do?

269
00:26:27,065 --> 00:26:30,015
It's you and me at the same time.

270
00:26:40,115 --> 00:26:42,565
The snake does not
abandon its nature, Kosses.

271
00:26:42,685 --> 00:26:46,635
I trust a man I don't know
more than Nicola.

272
00:26:48,055 --> 00:26:50,165
And I'm the one who knows Nikola the best.

273
00:26:51,115 --> 00:26:56,225
I know when, where, and how he will
stab us in the back.

274
00:26:56,995 --> 00:26:58,775
He is totally a snake!

275
00:26:59,685 --> 00:27:01,225
But we must not forget...

276
00:27:01,505 --> 00:27:04,735
...that there are eagle claws
on top of that snake.

277
00:27:06,455 --> 00:27:07,795
Eyvallah.

278
00:27:08,135 --> 00:27:11,635
We'll talk about these subjects in detail
when Osman Bey comes.

279
00:27:11,755 --> 00:27:13,145
Of course.

280
00:27:14,565 --> 00:27:18,155
He didn't say where he went,
but he'll come eventually.

281
00:27:25,915 --> 00:27:27,465
Osman Bey is coming!

282
00:27:47,265 --> 00:27:51,455
Come, there are important topics
that I will tell you about.

283
00:27:51,975 --> 00:27:53,565
Osman Bey.

284
00:28:01,335 --> 00:28:03,965
If you'll excuse me,
I also have something to tell you

285
00:28:10,935 --> 00:28:12,255
Come here

286
00:28:17,655 --> 00:28:20,445
My Bey, it's the merchant taxes in Sogut.

287
00:28:24,895 --> 00:28:26,275
Well done Erdogdu.

288
00:28:28,745 --> 00:28:30,315
But it doesn't belong here.

289
00:28:31,015 --> 00:28:34,465
See if there are any needy people
in the tribe and Sogut.

290
00:28:35,205 --> 00:28:36,975
And distribute the rest to the Ahis.

291
00:28:39,665 --> 00:28:43,395
And tell Alps to always be on alert.

292
00:28:46,055 --> 00:28:47,835
Excuse me, my Bey...

293
00:28:48,935 --> 00:28:52,615
While the Kayi and other tribes
are having hard times,

294
00:28:52,615 --> 00:28:55,835
what's the point of distributing
money to other tribes?

295
00:28:55,835 --> 00:29:01,315
What the Kayi tribe needs most in
this time is praying.

296
00:29:03,455 --> 00:29:08,285
The prayer of the needy is
more valuable than all money

297
00:29:10,425 --> 00:29:13,425
In addition, Ahis use their
shares in trading.

298
00:29:13,745 --> 00:29:15,285
They benefit Sogut.

299
00:29:18,915 --> 00:29:22,505
As the Bey of Kayi,
I say this is appropriate.

300
00:29:27,335 --> 00:29:29,835
The command is Gunduz Bey's.

301
00:29:38,955 --> 00:29:41,975
Erdogdu, don't forget what I said.

302
00:29:42,555 --> 00:29:44,085
Your command, my Bey.

303
00:30:00,285 --> 00:30:01,585
My Gunduz?

304
00:30:05,245 --> 00:30:07,535
Why didn't you take the Kayi taxes?

305
00:30:10,635 --> 00:30:13,135
So that they don't ask for it too.

306
00:30:16,625 --> 00:30:18,405
Vizier Alam Shah.

307
00:30:20,795 --> 00:30:22,885
United with ignoble Geyhatu.

308
00:30:24,315 --> 00:30:26,735
They will attack the rebellious
Turkmen tribes

309
00:30:29,455 --> 00:30:31,195
He asks for my valiant alps.

310
00:30:31,455 --> 00:30:33,195
What are you saying, Gunduz?

311
00:30:39,625 --> 00:30:41,325
There is no turning back of this.

312
00:30:43,025 --> 00:30:45,245
How am I going to get out of this?

313
00:30:50,895 --> 00:30:52,445
I heard Vizier.

314
00:30:53,665 --> 00:30:56,455
They will take over
all the castles, up to Iznik.

315
00:30:58,335 --> 00:30:59,835
And there's more.

316
00:31:01,165 --> 00:31:05,205
Gunduz Bey will give alps and horses
to Geyhatu...

317
00:31:06,635 --> 00:31:12,615
...in order to stop the rebellion in
Turkmen tribes.

318
00:31:13,395 --> 00:31:17,145
And Gunduz Bey will rule the castles
in the name of them.

319
00:31:23,605 --> 00:31:25,825
Gunduz Bey.

320
00:31:27,315 --> 00:31:30,355
The betrayal you committed is beyond Kayi.

321
00:31:30,945 --> 00:31:33,195
It reached all the Turks!

322
00:31:41,155 --> 00:31:42,865
Do you know...

323
00:31:45,055 --> 00:31:48,175
...why Geyhatu does this?

324
00:31:51,485 --> 00:31:54,225
Why does he want Kayi alps...

325
00:31:54,225 --> 00:31:59,935
despite of the arrival of 20,000 Mongol
soldiers sent by Arghun Khan?

326
00:32:00,755 --> 00:32:02,325
His intention is to...

327
00:32:03,905 --> 00:32:07,705
To show that the Kayi and the cruels
are alike.

328
00:32:08,155 --> 00:32:13,105
To killing the seeds of the state that we
will establish before they green!

329
00:32:18,065 --> 00:32:20,765
Who will believe the one who works with
the cruels?

330
00:32:21,635 --> 00:32:23,985
Who will trust their promises?

331
00:32:27,555 --> 00:32:30,255
These Mongol soldiers will
not enter Sogut.

332
00:32:30,675 --> 00:32:36,145
Even if they reach our lands,
they will not get out of here alive

333
00:32:39,655 --> 00:32:41,845
Listen carefully to what I have to say.

334
00:32:42,615 --> 00:32:46,445
The soldiers of the Lords will be
on a wing...

335
00:32:47,665 --> 00:32:51,815
Turgut Bey, you will be with your alps
on the other wing.

336
00:32:55,675 --> 00:32:57,825
Listen to me carefully.

337
00:32:59,505 --> 00:33:02,485
They will never pass from here.

338
00:33:03,405 --> 00:33:04,615
Never.

339
00:33:07,935 --> 00:33:09,605
We will be martyred, Osman Bey.

340
00:33:11,265 --> 00:33:14,245
Since I stood by you, Osman Bey.

341
00:33:14,765 --> 00:33:17,975
I abandoned my loved ones and
my life.

342
00:33:18,755 --> 00:33:20,185
The only truth now...

343
00:33:21,045 --> 00:33:23,085
...is martyrdom for the country.

344
00:33:29,965 --> 00:33:32,065
I don't have a castle anymore

345
00:33:33,755 --> 00:33:38,685
I don't know how loyal
my people to me now.

346
00:33:40,495 --> 00:33:44,255
But I am loyal enough to die for them.

347
00:33:45,835 --> 00:33:48,155
We will stop them, Osman Bey.

348
00:33:48,845 --> 00:33:50,175
Together.

349
00:33:53,465 --> 00:33:55,035
Being together...

350
00:33:56,275 --> 00:33:58,305
Boosts my confidence.

351
00:34:01,205 --> 00:34:02,585
Eyvallah.

352
00:34:03,125 --> 00:34:04,475
Eyvallah.

353
00:34:05,685 --> 00:34:07,215
But Nikola...

354
00:34:08,344 --> 00:34:09,895
I don't trust him.

355
00:34:10,505 --> 00:34:14,605
What if he doesn't send his soldiers?
What if he leaves us?

356
00:34:15,574 --> 00:34:18,795
We will be deficient, Osman Bey.

357
00:34:20,995 --> 00:34:22,605
He'll send.

358
00:34:27,025 --> 00:34:30,465
My Bey, Rogatus is here.

359
00:34:30,835 --> 00:34:32,155
Let him come.

360
00:34:39,074 --> 00:34:41,045
They did not allow me to enter Nikea.

361
00:34:42,344 --> 00:34:44,395
They didn't consider me a Lord.

362
00:34:45,125 --> 00:34:47,205
They said I don't have a castle.

363
00:34:59,035 --> 00:35:00,365
I know.

364
00:35:01,905 --> 00:35:03,275
I know.

365
00:35:03,965 --> 00:35:06,175
Then why did you send me if you knew?

366
00:35:07,265 --> 00:35:09,475
I wanted you to go and
see with your own eyes.

367
00:35:11,545 --> 00:35:14,635
That you can't do anything without me.

368
00:35:19,025 --> 00:35:25,885
I will give you back your Lordship,
your castle, and your soldiers.

369
00:35:29,925 --> 00:35:32,795
I wanted to make sure of your sincerity.

370
00:35:34,545 --> 00:35:37,355
My sincerity
didn't need this, Osman Bey.

371
00:35:37,875 --> 00:35:39,925
Go to Nicola now.

372
00:35:40,345 --> 00:35:41,915
He will tell you something important.

373
00:35:43,035 --> 00:35:45,595
Turahan Alp will join you too.

374
00:35:46,195 --> 00:35:48,975
He will tell you what to do.

375
00:35:58,815 --> 00:36:00,535
Turgut, you go as well.

376
00:36:06,735 --> 00:36:08,295
Not with them, go to the tribe.

377
00:36:09,515 --> 00:36:12,255
There's some important news
that Mari will tell you about.

378
00:36:13,815 --> 00:36:15,325
Be careful.

379
00:36:23,295 --> 00:36:26,295
Sogut.

380
00:36:26,505 --> 00:36:30,045
Nobody knows you came here except for
your Bey, right?

381
00:36:30,145 --> 00:36:33,235
I hid myself even from the birds
on my way here.

382
00:36:33,415 --> 00:36:37,065
You should hide from them more
at this time.

383
00:36:37,865 --> 00:36:39,385
The situation is not good.

384
00:36:39,385 --> 00:36:43,025
We departed on this road in order to break
the unfornute, Vizier Alam Shah

385
00:36:43,025 --> 00:36:44,795
There will certainly be difficulties.

386
00:36:44,795 --> 00:36:46,515
It's not difficulty.

387
00:36:46,815 --> 00:36:49,085
If we can't pervent it in time...

388
00:36:49,455 --> 00:36:50,835
It will be our end.

389
00:36:53,265 --> 00:36:56,485
20,000 Mongol soldiers who are
coming to Geyhatu...

390
00:36:56,655 --> 00:36:59,175
...will raid your Bey...

391
00:36:59,375 --> 00:37:03,685
...after they complete their work here.

392
00:37:04,915 --> 00:37:09,995
That they reach there means
the end for all of us.

393
00:37:10,455 --> 00:37:12,485
We'll stop them in time then.

394
00:37:12,805 --> 00:37:15,885
What do you think to do, Vizier Alam Shah?

395
00:37:17,075 --> 00:37:22,785
I will set Geyhatu up in a way that
he has never seen in his life.

396
00:37:24,505 --> 00:37:29,925
His filthy soldiers wil
l never trample our lands.

397
00:37:30,275 --> 00:37:36,035
My Bey's confidence in you is infinite,
Vizier Alam Shah, may Allah help you.

398
00:37:36,955 --> 00:37:38,275
Eyvallah.

399
00:37:38,565 --> 00:37:39,595
Eyvallah.

400
00:37:47,115 --> 00:37:50,485
Inegol Castle.

401
00:37:52,445 --> 00:37:57,325
It means that Samuel has been
with Kosses since the beginning.

402
00:37:58,035 --> 00:38:03,055
Well, how could you not see this, Argos?

403
00:38:11,375 --> 00:38:12,885
No, no!

404
00:38:15,705 --> 00:38:17,865
They took my sword at the door.

405
00:38:18,085 --> 00:38:19,665
You can calm down.

406
00:38:27,445 --> 00:38:30,005
What are you doing here?

407
00:38:35,215 --> 00:38:37,685
So, it means that the situation
is very dangerous.

408
00:38:38,485 --> 00:38:41,955
- So Osman deceived us all.
- No.

409
00:38:42,755 --> 00:38:44,795
Osman does not deceive anyone.

410
00:38:45,825 --> 00:38:48,125
You're on the right side, be sure of this.

411
00:39:06,350 --> 00:39:08,150
Osman Bey asked me to inform you.

412
00:39:09,620 --> 00:39:12,160
Geyhatu, Vizier Alam Shah and Gunduz Bey.

413
00:39:12,510 --> 00:39:15,780
They intend to take over all
the castles including Inegol Castle

414
00:39:16,670 --> 00:39:19,510
After they have taken
over the castles of all the Lords...

415
00:39:20,030 --> 00:39:24,140
They will leave the Mongol soldiers in the
borders of Inegol and attack Karamanogullari.

416
00:39:24,140 --> 00:39:27,400
Osman Bey has birds everywhere.

417
00:39:28,000 --> 00:39:30,210
He knows everything right away.

418
00:39:30,470 --> 00:39:35,720
My Bey knows every breath the infidels
breathe, from your lands to Mount Tengri.

419
00:39:39,050 --> 00:39:40,710
We are grateful.

420
00:39:42,120 --> 00:39:43,490
You can get out.

421
00:39:51,930 --> 00:39:54,590
I want you to stay here tonight, Rogatus.

422
00:39:55,230 --> 00:39:58,900
You'll take my soldiers
to Kosses and Turgut in the morning.

423
00:39:59,100 --> 00:40:02,400
Turgut is the commander of
this strange army.

424
00:40:03,750 --> 00:40:06,150
You will also carry out his commands.

425
00:40:06,150 --> 00:40:07,650
Literally.

426
00:40:08,680 --> 00:40:10,380
What does this mean?

427
00:40:10,940 --> 00:40:13,080
I will not serve under a
Turkish commander!

428
00:40:14,650 --> 00:40:19,710
I thought you were very happy to
have Osman next to you, Rogatus.

429
00:40:22,130 --> 00:40:23,890
He wanted this.

430
00:40:24,680 --> 00:40:26,430
You will abide by.

431
00:40:31,860 --> 00:40:37,080
That means
we'll put up with Turgut until this is over.

432
00:40:54,830 --> 00:40:56,410
My Mari.

433
00:40:56,500 --> 00:40:57,830
Turgut.

434
00:41:01,400 --> 00:41:03,160
I miss you from the heart.

435
00:41:05,270 --> 00:41:06,580
Me too.

436
00:41:14,480 --> 00:41:18,570
Osman Bey said that you were waiting for me
and you were to tell me something.

437
00:41:18,760 --> 00:41:20,130
Are you fine?

438
00:41:20,910 --> 00:41:22,450
Turgut.

439
00:41:24,450 --> 00:41:29,150
From now on, your eyes will not only
shine like a star when you look at me .

440
00:41:29,150 --> 00:41:31,450
but also when you look at her/him.

441
00:41:46,250 --> 00:41:47,640
I'm pregnant

442
00:41:51,550 --> 00:41:54,080
We will have a child, Turgut

443
00:41:56,670 --> 00:41:58,060
A child?

444
00:41:58,710 --> 00:42:00,040
...You are....

445
00:42:01,320 --> 00:42:03,110
Did you say a child?

446
00:42:04,050 --> 00:42:05,590
how?

447
00:42:06,370 --> 00:42:07,930
...We are now

448
00:42:08,520 --> 00:42:09,890
...I

449
00:42:09,960 --> 00:42:11,230
Will I be a father?

450
00:42:11,400 --> 00:42:12,760
Yes

451
00:42:20,400 --> 00:42:21,700
Thank Allah.

452
00:42:22,440 --> 00:42:24,950
Thank Allah, Mary, thank Allah.

453
00:42:26,990 --> 00:42:28,290
Thank Allah

454
00:42:30,100 --> 00:42:32,230
You will be a father, Turgut Bey!

455
00:42:33,500 --> 00:42:35,030
I will be a father.

456
00:42:36,710 --> 00:42:38,490
I'm going to be a father.

457
00:42:46,880 --> 00:42:48,210
But I...

458
00:42:49,370 --> 00:42:51,150
How will I protect you now?

459
00:42:53,400 --> 00:42:54,430
The Mongols are coming.

460
00:42:55,050 --> 00:42:59,540
I will not entrust you to Gunduz who
handed you over...

461
00:42:59,540 --> 00:43:01,890
to Vizier at the first opportunity.

462
00:43:06,060 --> 00:43:07,620
I'll take you to a safe place

463
00:43:08,220 --> 00:43:10,280
...we'll be separated for a while, but...

464
00:43:10,490 --> 00:43:11,820
Understand me.

465
00:43:11,880 --> 00:43:13,460
If something happens to you...

466
00:43:13,630 --> 00:43:16,070
I will burn myself and
this world with me, Mary

467
00:43:16,070 --> 00:43:17,260
Understand me.

468
00:43:18,300 --> 00:43:20,340
If you will come eventually...

469
00:43:20,720 --> 00:43:22,750
I will always wait for you, Turgut.

470
00:43:23,140 --> 00:43:24,710
I will definitely come.

471
00:43:25,270 --> 00:43:32,090
My mind and heart will always be with you

472
00:43:34,150 --> 00:43:35,700
Come on, get ready.

473
00:43:35,700 --> 00:43:37,490
Let's get out of here quickly.

474
00:43:37,510 --> 00:43:38,870
Okay.

475
00:43:40,120 --> 00:43:41,480
Let's og.

476
00:44:27,340 --> 00:44:29,110
Is that your number?

477
00:44:30,140 --> 00:44:31,430
There is no shortage.

478
00:44:32,480 --> 00:44:33,790
We are complete.

479
00:44:38,450 --> 00:44:41,220
Are you going out like this
in front of our emperor?

480
00:44:43,520 --> 00:44:45,180
We're going to talk.

481
00:44:46,470 --> 00:44:48,700
No need for a large number of people
to speak.

482
00:44:51,020 --> 00:44:56,170
We have what we need.

483
00:44:59,970 --> 00:45:02,890
Excuse my curiosity, Osman Bey.

484
00:45:07,560 --> 00:45:11,990
How do you know that the emperor
will trust you and won't kill you?

485
00:45:13,650 --> 00:45:20,610
Today, the emperor will decide whether
Constantinople will be...

486
00:45:20,610 --> 00:45:23,010
...Turks' or Mongols'.

487
00:45:51,290 --> 00:45:52,850
Osman.

488
00:45:53,830 --> 00:45:57,360
I will kill your loved ones one by one.

489
00:45:57,990 --> 00:45:59,540
And then you.

490
00:46:08,890 --> 00:46:10,230
Malhun.

491
00:46:12,050 --> 00:46:13,820
So, it's your turn.

492
00:46:15,000 --> 00:46:16,720
You will die today.

493
00:46:21,680 --> 00:46:24,240
Come on, we'll follow them.

494
00:47:24,310 --> 00:47:28,430
Today there is a cannibal in my share.

495
00:47:56,230 --> 00:47:59,510
The bird, the bird!

496
00:48:31,650 --> 00:48:33,170
You're hungry, cannibal, aren't you?

497
00:48:35,430 --> 00:48:36,690
You are hungry

498
00:48:39,470 --> 00:48:40,750
Eat it!

499
00:48:44,670 --> 00:48:46,190
Won't you eat?

500
00:48:48,090 --> 00:48:49,390
Okay.

501
00:48:49,890 --> 00:48:51,250
As you like.

502
00:48:59,550 --> 00:49:03,130
You shouldn't have touched the bird.

503
00:50:01,790 --> 00:50:03,130
Welcome.

504
00:50:03,130 --> 00:50:05,250
I brought your army to be at your command.

505
00:50:05,370 --> 00:50:06,910
Turgut Bey.

506
00:50:09,770 --> 00:50:11,070
Eyvallah (thank you)

507
00:50:18,390 --> 00:50:20,130
Don't do this my old friend.

508
00:50:20,630 --> 00:50:22,350
You are still a religious man.

509
00:50:22,510 --> 00:50:25,670
Protecting our people is
your primary mission.

510
00:50:27,950 --> 00:50:30,670
And Turgut Bey will help
us succeed in this.

511
00:50:35,190 --> 00:50:37,210
I don't say this because he is my family.

512
00:50:37,310 --> 00:50:38,690
Do not worry

513
00:50:39,090 --> 00:50:40,590
He's a good leader.

514
00:50:40,610 --> 00:50:42,150
And a brave soldier.

515
00:50:50,930 --> 00:50:54,510
I only protect my citizens.

516
00:50:57,430 --> 00:51:00,670
However, since
the majority made such a decision...

517
00:51:04,130 --> 00:51:06,710
I am at your command, Turgut Bey.

518
00:51:11,830 --> 00:51:13,390
I'm honored, Rogatus.

519
00:51:16,790 --> 00:51:18,970
Your standing with us will
make us stronger.

520
00:51:21,590 --> 00:51:23,310
Since you are with us...

521
00:51:26,190 --> 00:51:27,490
Eyvallah (thank you).

522
00:51:34,150 --> 00:51:35,470
So...

523
00:51:36,010 --> 00:51:37,730
What do we do now?

524
00:51:38,390 --> 00:51:40,470
Shall we attack without wasting time?

525
00:51:42,890 --> 00:51:44,930
The attack has already started.

526
00:51:45,710 --> 00:51:49,310
The game I set up is currently
running without any problems.

527
00:51:59,090 --> 00:52:01,010
The situation is bad, my Bey.

528
00:52:01,590 --> 00:52:03,370
Geyhatu is coming with his soldiers.

529
00:52:03,610 --> 00:52:05,150
And Vizier is with im.

530
00:52:06,730 --> 00:52:08,470
They are very crowded.

531
00:52:10,610 --> 00:52:11,950
Geyhatu.

532
00:53:00,090 --> 00:53:04,850
For the sons and daughters of Erlik Khan.

533
00:53:31,350 --> 00:53:34,210
For the sons and daughters of Erlik Khan.

534
00:53:40,530 --> 00:53:44,270
For the sons and daughters of Erlik Khan.

535
00:54:26,950 --> 00:54:28,430
Welcome, Geyhatu.

536
00:54:31,410 --> 00:54:35,910
The best commander of Argun Khan.

537
00:54:38,410 --> 00:54:39,930
That's for sure.

538
00:54:40,750 --> 00:54:46,610
For the sons and daughters of Erlik Khan.

539
00:54:47,170 --> 00:54:50,870
We've brought the Greek fire,
we'll burn the walls.

540
00:54:50,870 --> 00:54:52,870
The castles of the Lords will become ours.

541
00:56:26,910 --> 00:56:29,170
The war will begin.

542
00:56:30,110 --> 00:56:32,670
There will be a lot of blood.

543
00:56:33,670 --> 00:56:38,810
A lot of blood for Erlik Khan.

544
00:56:45,590 --> 00:56:46,730
Damn it.

545
00:56:48,090 --> 00:56:50,130
We can't attack while Geyhatu is there.

546
00:56:51,010 --> 00:56:52,510
It will be our end.

547
00:56:53,370 --> 00:56:54,990
But we must find a way.

548
00:56:55,370 --> 00:56:57,550
Osman Bey trusts me.

549
00:56:57,990 --> 00:57:03,690
I'd rather this to be my last war than
not keep the promise I made to him.

550
00:57:05,130 --> 00:57:06,950
And let my death be at
the hands Mongols.

551
00:57:09,970 --> 00:57:13,030
Also, while Cerkutay is there...

552
00:57:14,010 --> 00:57:16,210
...we cannot go back because
Geyhatu has come

553
00:57:17,490 --> 00:57:19,650
Do not order us to retreat, Turgut Bey.

554
00:57:19,910 --> 00:57:21,530
We can die but we cannot retreat.

555
00:57:25,790 --> 00:57:27,290
Don't worry, Turahan.

556
00:57:27,650 --> 00:57:30,410
We can die but we cannot retreat.

557
00:57:33,870 --> 00:57:35,570
You'll get used to it, my old friend.

558
00:57:36,410 --> 00:57:39,170
Look at me, do I ever get surprised?

559
00:57:57,550 --> 00:57:59,310
It's Konur, Alps.

560
00:58:11,550 --> 00:58:13,330
I will help you.

561
00:58:22,870 --> 00:58:24,210
How?

562
00:58:28,085 --> 00:58:30,140
Sogut.

563
00:58:33,485 --> 00:58:35,425
Now that we are in the bazaar...

564
00:58:35,425 --> 00:58:37,425
We should buy whatever you need, Aygül.

565
00:58:37,865 --> 00:58:40,465
As you know, the return of my Osman Bey
is soon.

566
00:58:41,845 --> 00:58:44,705
You take care of me with all your worries.

567
00:58:45,285 --> 00:58:46,945
Thank you, Malhun.

568
00:58:46,945 --> 00:58:51,705
My mother is determined. We'll have
your wedding once they return.

569
00:58:51,905 --> 00:58:54,425
Inshallah, they will come back safely.

570
00:59:00,145 --> 00:59:01,505
Come.

571
00:59:10,765 --> 00:59:12,935
- Demonstrate that one, will you?
- Of course

572
00:59:12,935 --> 00:59:14,785
This color here is more vivid.

573
00:59:22,105 --> 00:59:24,145
This color suits you so much.

574
00:59:47,405 --> 00:59:49,165
What is going on here?

575
01:00:20,825 --> 01:00:22,565
Let's see that one too.

576
01:00:48,485 --> 01:00:49,865
Boran!

577
01:01:00,665 --> 01:01:02,045
Take these.

578
01:01:02,045 --> 01:01:03,145
Eyvallah (okay).

579
01:01:03,145 --> 01:01:05,145
Come on, brothers.

580
01:01:09,525 --> 01:01:10,865
Let's go.

581
01:02:04,385 --> 01:02:06,925
Sir, Konur arrived.

582
01:02:09,865 --> 01:02:12,985
No one was to know that
we would be here, Vizier.

583
01:02:14,725 --> 01:02:16,785
There is clearly something important.

584
01:02:18,485 --> 01:02:20,265
Let him come.

585
01:02:34,345 --> 01:02:36,125
Is everything okay, Konur?

586
01:02:36,165 --> 01:02:37,745
I told you to stay in the inn.

587
01:02:38,045 --> 01:02:39,415
Why did you come?

588
01:02:39,415 --> 01:02:41,915
I wouldn't have come if it wasn't
important, Vizier.

589
01:02:41,915 --> 01:02:43,215
Osman.

590
01:02:46,745 --> 01:02:48,345
I've been following him
since the night.

591
01:02:49,465 --> 01:02:51,505
I found the place they stay.

592
01:02:55,565 --> 01:02:57,125
But they are crowded.

593
01:02:57,685 --> 01:02:59,065
I couldn't attack them.

594
01:03:02,665 --> 01:03:04,885
How crowded could they be?

595
01:03:06,565 --> 01:03:09,365
They are helpless against the
Mongol soldiers!

596
01:03:12,805 --> 01:03:14,625
Soldiers! Move!

597
01:03:31,405 --> 01:03:32,705
My Bey!

598
01:03:34,085 --> 01:03:38,825
My Bey, Konor Alp, took Geyhatu and Vizier
out among the soldiers.

599
01:03:40,025 --> 01:03:41,345
Thank him.

600
01:03:44,145 --> 01:03:45,845
Now, it's time to act.

601
01:03:46,525 --> 01:03:48,045
Get everyone ready

602
01:03:48,665 --> 01:03:50,225
We will attack!

603
01:03:51,925 --> 01:03:53,965
No mercy on Mongols!

604
01:03:54,185 --> 01:03:56,205
If necessary, we will die!

605
01:03:58,555 --> 01:04:01,145
Around Iznik Castle.

606
01:04:06,645 --> 01:04:08,185
Let's rest a bit here.

607
01:04:35,225 --> 01:04:38,245
This place is better for resting.

608
01:05:07,425 --> 01:05:08,785
Take this.

609
01:05:11,285 --> 01:05:14,865
All exits and entrances to the castle
were drawn here.

610
01:05:15,865 --> 01:05:19,985
Examine which road is better and
which way is safer.

611
01:05:20,845 --> 01:05:24,285
Confirm the accuracy of the entrances and
exits of the castle.

612
01:05:24,285 --> 01:05:26,545
If not, draw a new one.

613
01:05:26,785 --> 01:05:28,145
My Bey.

614
01:05:30,785 --> 01:05:32,545
You saw my tent.

615
01:06:35,945 --> 01:06:38,105
Oh, what a shepherd you are!

616
01:06:39,585 --> 01:06:42,415
Do you think you're the only one
who knows how to hide?

617
01:06:43,745 --> 01:06:45,105
My Bey.

618
01:06:46,025 --> 01:06:48,315
I was waiting for the right
time to tell you

619
01:06:49,785 --> 01:06:51,545
But I've been exposed.

620
01:06:56,385 --> 01:06:58,185
We ask you your name...

621
01:06:59,065 --> 01:07:00,845
All you say is " I am shepherd."

622
01:07:02,865 --> 01:07:04,425
Tell me.

623
01:07:13,685 --> 01:07:15,405
My mother named me Akca.

624
01:07:16,565 --> 01:07:18,345
and put faith in my heart.

625
01:07:19,505 --> 01:07:21,225
My father taught me to ride a horse.

626
01:07:22,545 --> 01:07:24,545
And taught me how to use a sword.

627
01:07:27,565 --> 01:07:29,585
I was a shepherd who had a herd.

628
01:07:32,245 --> 01:07:36,245
One day, Lord's dogs
raided my herd, my Bey.

629
01:07:37,565 --> 01:07:38,925
My father

630
01:07:40,605 --> 01:07:42,165
My father, my Bey...

631
01:07:42,725 --> 01:07:45,285
My father was martyred,
and I was captured.

632
01:07:47,005 --> 01:07:49,845
They gave me to an Armenian carpenter,
and he educated me.

633
01:07:53,005 --> 01:07:55,045
But I am Turkish, Osman Bey.

634
01:07:55,525 --> 01:07:57,045
I will not be captivated.

635
01:07:58,245 --> 01:08:00,025
My heart is always free.

636
01:08:01,305 --> 01:08:03,585
I painted every detail in order to escape.

637
01:08:04,165 --> 01:08:06,245
There is not a single stone that
I do not know.

638
01:08:10,385 --> 01:08:11,705
I said...

639
01:08:12,445 --> 01:08:16,545
One day I will attack these walls...

640
01:08:17,965 --> 01:08:19,725
I swore.

641
01:08:22,185 --> 01:08:25,245
My Bey, I've been waiting for you to
make this moment real.

642
01:08:26,904 --> 01:08:30,965
And one day you came as a wounded Turk
and entered in the midst of my herd!

643
01:08:33,564 --> 01:08:35,265
Thank Allah, my Bey.

644
01:08:41,845 --> 01:08:44,404
When the path we walk is one...

645
01:08:45,365 --> 01:08:47,904
It was always possible
that we would meet, Akca.

646
01:08:48,645 --> 01:08:51,205
Right people will be on the right path.

647
01:08:53,305 --> 01:08:54,645
Do they...

648
01:08:55,845 --> 01:08:57,404
...do they know, my Bey?

649
01:09:07,805 --> 01:09:09,145
My Bey...

650
01:09:09,524 --> 01:09:12,104
Ignore my sanity, or insanity.

651
01:09:12,904 --> 01:09:14,944
It is difficult sometimes.

652
01:09:14,944 --> 01:09:16,944
No.

653
01:09:17,345 --> 01:09:19,185
You don't control your mind.

654
01:09:20,345 --> 01:09:25,125
So that we conquer all the castles!

655
01:09:28,564 --> 01:09:30,125
Eyvallah, my Bey.

656
01:09:31,765 --> 01:09:35,965
I will be by your side all the life
that my Creator gives me

657
01:09:45,645 --> 01:09:46,984
Osman Bey.

658
01:09:51,285 --> 01:09:54,885
The emperor protects
his castle with the best soldiers.

659
01:09:57,210 --> 01:10:00,080
Do you think they will let the
brave, rebel...

660
01:10:00,080 --> 01:10:02,330
...yet a former Bey of Kayi?

661
01:10:05,945 --> 01:10:08,325
Until I die...

662
01:10:10,405 --> 01:10:13,165
...I am the Bey of Kayı, Nikola.

663
01:10:15,505 --> 01:10:16,805
You will see.

664
01:10:18,005 --> 01:10:21,585
I will get dangerously close to
the Emperor.

665
01:10:22,305 --> 01:10:26,465
So, all those soldiers in the castle will
let you in without a doubt.

666
01:10:26,745 --> 01:10:28,125
Is that so?

667
01:10:28,325 --> 01:10:30,345
Why do you think I brought you with me?

668
01:10:35,485 --> 01:10:36,825
What is it in your mind?

669
01:10:37,905 --> 01:10:41,925
You will introduce me as a spy you sent
among the Turks.

670
01:10:44,945 --> 01:10:47,665
No one will know who I am...

671
01:10:49,505 --> 01:10:52,625
...until we meet the Emperor.

672
01:10:55,765 --> 01:10:58,345
Osman Bey!

673
01:12:00,205 --> 01:12:04,045
For Erlik Khan's sons and daughters!

674
01:12:05,105 --> 01:12:08,705
For Erlik Khan's sons and daughters!

675
01:12:16,525 --> 01:12:21,745
Cannibal dogs!

676
01:12:42,985 --> 01:12:45,265
Governor Saguros is not available.

677
01:12:45,265 --> 01:12:48,925
I came to meet the Emperor,
not Governor Saguros.

678
01:12:51,325 --> 01:12:52,865
Nikola!

679
01:12:54,765 --> 01:12:56,285
Eldoris!

680
01:12:57,525 --> 01:12:59,685
The closest to the Emperor...

681
01:12:59,925 --> 01:13:01,485
...Eldoris!

682
01:13:06,285 --> 01:13:07,865
What are you doing here?

683
01:13:07,865 --> 01:13:10,745
Let's say I want to be close to
the Emperor like you.

684
01:13:13,665 --> 01:13:17,165
Emperor Andronikos is here but no one
knows.

685
01:13:18,985 --> 01:13:21,565
You are accessing information that doesn't
concern you.

686
01:13:23,125 --> 01:13:27,185
We came here with crucial information,
Eldoris.

687
01:13:27,185 --> 01:13:29,185
Can you inform the Emperor?

688
01:13:29,645 --> 01:13:31,025
Please.

689
01:13:37,605 --> 01:13:39,365
Who is this?

690
01:13:39,385 --> 01:13:42,885
He is a spy I put among the Turks much
time ago.

691
01:13:42,885 --> 01:13:45,265
He also knows information that doesn't
concern him.

692
01:13:47,005 --> 01:13:49,925
He wants to share them only with
the Emperor.

693
01:13:54,185 --> 01:13:55,545
No!

694
01:13:57,365 --> 01:13:59,685
Only you, Nikola.

695
01:14:02,505 --> 01:14:04,785
Even the reason he is here is me.

696
01:14:05,885 --> 01:14:07,925
I will only tell it to the Emperor.

697
01:14:09,065 --> 01:14:11,105
Even Nikola doesn't know.

698
01:14:12,345 --> 01:14:15,385
So he is an important enough spy to
call you by your name.

699
01:14:18,425 --> 01:14:19,785
Really...

700
01:14:20,365 --> 01:14:21,665
...who are you?

701
01:14:22,885 --> 01:14:27,385
I'm the one who will save your castles
from falling to Mongolian.

702
01:14:32,745 --> 01:14:34,245
Eldoris...

703
01:14:34,965 --> 01:14:36,345
...the Emperor.

704
01:15:06,065 --> 01:15:07,825
Mighty Emperor Andronikos...

705
01:15:07,825 --> 01:15:10,905
...I know you don't want to get
interrupted while working but...

706
01:15:10,905 --> 01:15:12,905
Cut it short, Eldoris.
Speak.

707
01:15:14,265 --> 01:15:17,705
The Lord of İnegöl, Aya Nikola wants
to see you.

708
01:15:18,045 --> 01:15:20,185
We have a huge information gap.

709
01:15:21,245 --> 01:15:22,565
Let him in.

710
01:15:24,185 --> 01:15:26,725
He is with an unknown Turk.

711
01:15:29,265 --> 01:15:30,965
He said that he is a spy.

712
01:15:31,625 --> 01:15:33,345
An unknown Turk?

713
01:15:51,425 --> 01:15:52,775
Honorable Emperor...

714
01:15:52,775 --> 01:15:56,155
...as if it wasn't enough for me to
be under the same sky as you...

715
01:15:56,165 --> 01:15:57,885
...now I'm here before you.

716
01:15:58,905 --> 01:16:00,285
I am honored.

717
01:16:00,685 --> 01:16:02,385
And I greet you with respect.

718
01:16:03,345 --> 01:16:05,465
How did you know I'm here, Nikola?

719
01:16:07,325 --> 01:16:09,185
I told him.

720
01:16:13,625 --> 01:16:14,745
Who are you?

721
01:16:15,525 --> 01:16:19,665
Osman Bey, son of Ertugrul Gazi.

722
01:16:26,285 --> 01:16:27,285
Osman!

723
01:16:37,825 --> 01:16:39,465
Don't, Osman!

724
01:16:40,625 --> 01:16:42,885
Don't!

725
01:16:42,885 --> 01:16:46,065
Open the door!
Open the door!

726
01:16:46,065 --> 01:16:48,345
Don't you dare make a mistake!

727
01:16:48,345 --> 01:16:50,345
Idiot Nikola!

728
01:16:50,345 --> 01:16:53,045
How can you get a Turk into my room!

729
01:16:53,145 --> 01:16:55,645
Open the door!

730
01:16:56,385 --> 01:16:57,905
Open the door!

731
01:17:00,805 --> 01:17:02,365
Open the door!

732
01:17:04,465 --> 01:17:06,025
Emperor!

733
01:17:06,025 --> 01:17:08,525
If my intention was to fight...

734
01:17:13,305 --> 01:17:14,805
Emperor!

735
01:17:22,285 --> 01:17:26,465
...there would be ten thousand horsemen
behind these walls.

736
01:17:33,505 --> 01:17:35,165
I just want to talk...

737
01:17:37,065 --> 01:17:38,565
...Emperor.

738
01:17:40,385 --> 01:17:42,665
Just to talk.

739
01:17:52,505 --> 01:17:53,725
Let him go.

740
01:18:14,605 --> 01:18:15,965
Come on!
Hurry!

741
01:18:49,205 --> 01:18:50,505
Come on!

742
01:18:58,245 --> 01:19:00,025
What happened here?

743
01:19:00,485 --> 01:19:02,025
Catch the horse!

744
01:19:12,145 --> 01:19:17,465
So, we will perish if we are not united
against the Mongols.

745
01:19:18,405 --> 01:19:21,085
I don't live in a tent, Osman.

746
01:19:21,345 --> 01:19:23,085
I have walls.

747
01:19:23,545 --> 01:19:27,345
I have waters guarded by a giant chain.

748
01:19:31,265 --> 01:19:34,365
When the day comes, all can be
dealt with, Your Imperial Highness.

749
01:19:35,425 --> 01:19:36,745
But let's say...

750
01:19:37,705 --> 01:19:39,865
...it keeps you safe for now.

751
01:19:41,745 --> 01:19:45,505
So how will you feed Constantinople...

752
01:19:46,625 --> 01:19:49,185
...when there is a massacre in the east?

753
01:19:51,285 --> 01:19:53,565
Your wheat is enough for you
only eight months.

754
01:19:54,065 --> 01:19:56,805
More than half of gutters need repairs.

755
01:19:59,445 --> 01:20:00,985
What about the army?

756
01:20:03,365 --> 01:20:06,365
It's not enough to quell a civil war.

757
01:20:07,345 --> 01:20:11,685
None of these things are a reason
for me to ally with you.

758
01:20:12,945 --> 01:20:14,325
Right..

759
01:20:15,945 --> 01:20:17,525
You are right.

760
01:20:18,965 --> 01:20:22,565
When the time comes, you make your
alliance with the Catholic Latins.

761
01:20:24,245 --> 01:20:26,785
They will save Constantinople.

762
01:20:33,685 --> 01:20:38,045
Or ask the Pope for a crusader army.

763
01:20:38,665 --> 01:20:40,345
Behave, Osman!

764
01:20:41,385 --> 01:20:44,665
It's not your place to talk about
my co-religionists.

765
01:20:44,665 --> 01:20:48,465
Moreover, the Mongols have not yet
reached my walls to besiege my city.

766
01:20:49,245 --> 01:20:53,965
You Muslims besieged the city
every chance you got.

767
01:20:55,865 --> 01:20:57,165
Maybe...

768
01:20:57,285 --> 01:20:59,285
...I should write a letter to
Argun Khan...

769
01:20:59,705 --> 01:21:03,405
...we should corner you between us
and destroy you.

770
01:21:04,305 --> 01:21:05,965
Your Imperial Highness...

771
01:21:07,385 --> 01:21:11,905
...we Muslims make a home from the lands
we conquer.

772
01:21:12,545 --> 01:21:14,785
We restore the places we conquer.

773
01:21:16,185 --> 01:21:18,185
What about the Mongols?

774
01:21:18,865 --> 01:21:24,685
When they come, they destroy the land
and kill everyone.

775
01:21:28,465 --> 01:21:31,965
Is it up to you to think about
the future of Constantinople?

776
01:21:34,685 --> 01:21:38,305
I take the troubles of all innocents
to myself, Your Imperial Highness.

777
01:21:42,585 --> 01:21:43,905
But...

778
01:21:45,505 --> 01:21:47,545
...if we don't stand together...

779
01:21:47,985 --> 01:21:50,805
...they will destroy all of us one by one.

780
01:21:52,525 --> 01:21:54,597
The Vanguard comes before...

781
01:21:54,788 --> 01:21:56,351
...the Army of twenty thousand.

782
01:21:58,015 --> 01:22:00,025
I would like to make a deal...

783
01:22:04,445 --> 01:22:05,995
...before facing them.

784
01:22:08,815 --> 01:22:11,355
I want to secure my back as I fight...

785
01:22:13,535 --> 01:22:15,285
...to the last drop of my blood.

786
01:22:19,025 --> 01:22:20,575
Therefore...

787
01:22:21,985 --> 01:22:27,055
...I want the castles taken from Rogatus
and Kosses to be given back.

788
01:22:30,335 --> 01:22:34,165
I want to graze my animals freely
in your pastures.

789
01:22:36,535 --> 01:22:37,925
And...

790
01:22:40,965 --> 01:22:43,005
...I want Nikola's loyalty.

791
01:22:47,245 --> 01:22:49,645
Since he got you all the way
into my room...

792
01:22:51,945 --> 01:22:54,255
...Nikola is already loyal to you.

793
01:23:02,165 --> 01:23:08,415
I want the other Lords at far away to
be under my command too.

794
01:23:21,425 --> 01:23:26,985
What if you can't succeed after having
such a great power, Osman Bey?

795
01:23:28,955 --> 01:23:32,215
Then you also will have destroyed
my strength of resistance.

796
01:23:33,765 --> 01:23:36,285
Everything has a point when you have
a cause.

797
01:23:38,485 --> 01:23:42,535
We fight for neither name nor glory.

798
01:23:45,585 --> 01:23:49,695
The only thing that matters to us
is the safety of people.

799
01:23:52,235 --> 01:23:54,235
If they pass us...

800
01:23:55,525 --> 01:23:58,605
...they won't even have the power to
come to you.

801
01:24:04,245 --> 01:24:07,325
You also will be rid of a Turk Bey.

802
01:24:11,805 --> 01:24:14,835
You will be winning, either way, Emperor.

803
01:24:18,805 --> 01:24:20,865
You will win.

804
01:24:44,975 --> 01:24:46,715
How did this happen?

805
01:24:56,855 --> 01:24:58,215
Choke it!

806
01:25:00,495 --> 01:25:02,065
Red Shaman.

807
01:25:48,835 --> 01:25:50,945
Trap!
Protect the chests!

808
01:25:50,945 --> 01:25:52,245
Come on!

809
01:26:05,135 --> 01:26:07,225
Your end is near, cannibal.

810
01:26:08,905 --> 01:26:10,265
Come on!

811
01:26:11,645 --> 01:26:13,005
Traitor!

812
01:26:19,295 --> 01:26:22,345
Choke it! Choke it!

813
01:26:23,275 --> 01:26:26,845
All right, I'll do that.

814
01:26:34,465 --> 01:26:36,195
No!

815
01:26:42,115 --> 01:26:47,285
Blood! Blood! Blood!

816
01:28:13,655 --> 01:28:15,005
It will be night soon.

817
01:28:15,885 --> 01:28:17,245
What if she changed her
mind?

818
01:28:19,665 --> 01:28:21,465
She will deal with it today.

819
01:28:23,105 --> 01:28:25,685
Obviously, attacking in the crowd
didn't work for her.

820
01:28:26,375 --> 01:28:28,265
She is not brave enough to face us.

821
01:28:30,125 --> 01:28:31,955
She can only go behind our backs.

822
01:28:32,515 --> 01:28:34,465
Vile dog!

823
01:28:41,885 --> 01:28:44,055
They are too crowded, we can't get close.

824
01:28:46,795 --> 01:28:48,945
Malhun will die today!

825
01:28:59,055 --> 01:29:01,115
Something is happening.

826
01:29:02,585 --> 01:29:04,155
You wait here.

827
01:29:04,185 --> 01:29:05,505
Come on.

828
01:29:12,005 --> 01:29:15,335
Malhun is leaving, alone.

829
01:29:15,935 --> 01:29:17,435
Go after her, now!

830
01:29:26,625 --> 01:29:28,695
Good job, brother Cerkutay.

831
01:29:29,315 --> 01:29:31,345
You are such a valiant.

832
01:29:32,365 --> 01:29:34,155
Congratulations, Cerkutay.

833
01:29:35,085 --> 01:29:39,865
Now I understand better why
Osman Bey trusted you his eyes closed.

834
01:29:42,295 --> 01:29:43,675
Thank you.

835
01:29:45,065 --> 01:29:46,395
Thank you.

836
01:29:49,145 --> 01:29:51,955
They brought chests of fire, Turgut Bey.

837
01:29:52,255 --> 01:29:54,395
They were going to break the walls
with these.

838
01:29:54,925 --> 01:29:57,195
They would destroy many castles.

839
01:29:59,575 --> 01:30:01,615
They protected them with their lives.

840
01:30:04,755 --> 01:30:06,345
They lost their lives.

841
01:30:07,815 --> 01:30:09,585
Now, we have the fire.

842
01:30:11,235 --> 01:30:14,435
Both the power and the danger are in
our palms.

843
01:30:15,305 --> 01:30:18,315
Geyhatu's wrinkled face will get
even more wrinkled...

844
01:30:18,315 --> 01:30:20,505
...when he hears this news.

845
01:30:25,135 --> 01:30:26,685
Get ready at once, Alps!

846
01:30:27,525 --> 01:30:30,915
We will go to Osman Bey and tell him
we got the fire.

847
01:30:33,265 --> 01:30:36,155
My Osman Bey will be the happiest
about this.

848
01:30:38,195 --> 01:30:39,545
Come on!

849
01:30:54,945 --> 01:30:56,325
My Bey...

850
01:30:56,885 --> 01:31:01,115
...I say we first hit İznik if they don't
accept the deal.

851
01:31:01,115 --> 01:31:02,575
They will accept it.

852
01:31:03,855 --> 01:31:09,835
I made sure they know what will happen
if they don't.

853
01:31:37,475 --> 01:31:38,855
Osman Bey.

854
01:31:40,405 --> 01:31:42,985
I was so sure the Emperor were going to
kill you.

855
01:31:48,445 --> 01:31:51,215
You were so sure that you would kill me
too.

856
01:31:54,865 --> 01:31:56,955
The Emperor trusts you.

857
01:32:01,855 --> 01:32:03,685
It's a sign of his trust.

858
01:32:11,035 --> 01:32:14,115
Until we banish Geyhatu from
these lands...

859
01:32:14,115 --> 01:32:18,175
...every Lord under my command will be
by your side, Osman Bey.

860
01:32:18,175 --> 01:32:20,305
Emperor Andronikos.

861
01:32:26,065 --> 01:32:28,355
I will be waiting to hear from you,
Osman Bey.

862
01:32:29,455 --> 01:32:31,455
Goodbye, for now.

863
01:32:31,455 --> 01:32:33,015
Be careful.

864
01:32:34,525 --> 01:32:36,245
The big battle is near.

865
01:32:39,635 --> 01:32:41,005
Soldiers!

866
01:33:48,515 --> 01:33:50,365
They have just moved.

867
01:33:50,625 --> 01:33:54,135
Clearly, his watchmen saw us coming.

868
01:34:04,165 --> 01:34:05,885
They went this way.

869
01:34:07,295 --> 01:34:08,645
The tracks are fresh.

870
01:34:08,915 --> 01:34:11,955
Spread around!
Search everywhere!

871
01:34:12,185 --> 01:34:14,755
Find Osman and follow him!

872
01:34:28,975 --> 01:34:30,835
Come on!
Come on!

873
01:34:42,715 --> 01:34:46,075
-Malhun!
-Julia!

874
01:34:50,855 --> 01:34:52,175
You dog!

875
01:34:59,385 --> 01:35:03,065
Welcome to your death, Malhun!

876
01:35:06,125 --> 01:35:08,315
You can handle me only when I am
alone, right?

877
01:35:08,565 --> 01:35:10,295
Why didn't you attack me at Söğüt?

878
01:35:10,295 --> 01:35:12,035
I don't like hard work.

879
01:35:12,995 --> 01:35:14,725
Now, you will die.

880
01:35:16,555 --> 01:35:20,635
You're wrong, Julia, It's not me who will
die today, it's you.

881
01:35:21,975 --> 01:35:25,985
But when you have the blood of many
innocent people in your hands...

882
01:35:26,325 --> 01:35:29,045
...your death won't be easy.

883
01:35:29,745 --> 01:35:31,115
Die!

884
01:35:40,165 --> 01:35:41,535
Boran!

885
01:35:42,115 --> 01:35:44,375
I came here to kill you, you dog!

886
01:35:44,835 --> 01:35:46,395
You will die today!

887
01:35:46,735 --> 01:35:48,975
-Trap!
-Come on, Alps!

888
01:36:19,095 --> 01:36:21,865
How did you catch me, Malhun?

889
01:36:22,785 --> 01:36:26,555
It wasn't hard at all, Julia.
At all.

890
01:36:27,735 --> 01:36:31,765
Come on, kill me!
Kill me!

891
01:36:32,085 --> 01:36:36,685
You will die but, you will die slowly!

892
01:36:56,855 --> 01:36:58,345
Praise be!

893
01:37:05,075 --> 01:37:06,685
For those you killed!

894
01:37:07,615 --> 01:37:08,685
Allahu Akbar!

895
01:37:08,685 --> 01:37:11,835
Boran, stop!

896
01:37:14,115 --> 01:37:17,135
Boran, I said stop!

897
01:37:18,095 --> 01:37:21,145
-Calm down!
-Boran!

898
01:37:24,375 --> 01:37:25,745
Boran!

899
01:37:31,635 --> 01:37:34,615
Boran!
Be patient!

900
01:37:35,465 --> 01:37:38,245
Listen to me!
Be patient!

901
01:37:52,205 --> 01:37:54,715
Söğüt

902
01:37:55,185 --> 01:38:00,365
Even if we didn't get results, your effort
is admirable, Konur.

903
01:38:00,645 --> 01:38:02,825
I am honored, my Vizier.

904
01:38:02,825 --> 01:38:04,215
Can I come in, my Vizier?

905
01:38:05,465 --> 01:38:06,815
Come in.

906
01:38:10,155 --> 01:38:13,825
My Vizier, Nikola sent news with his man.

907
01:38:13,965 --> 01:38:16,625
He will visit Geyhatu.

908
01:38:16,785 --> 01:38:19,755
He wishes you to join them.

909
01:38:22,215 --> 01:38:24,135
So, he is still alive.

910
01:38:24,725 --> 01:38:26,905
And he wants me to join, is that so?

911
01:38:27,495 --> 01:38:31,975
Nikola!
Nikola!

912
01:38:34,275 --> 01:38:37,995
If he wants that much I will join them.

913
01:38:38,675 --> 01:38:45,695
I will be there when Geyhatu tears
his filthy head from his body.

914
01:38:58,635 --> 01:38:59,675
Murderer!

915
01:38:59,675 --> 01:39:03,335
Murderer! Murderer! Killer
Murderer!

916
01:39:05,045 --> 01:39:08,295
Killer! Murderer!

917
01:39:09,355 --> 01:39:12,445
Dog! Killer! Murderer!

918
01:39:12,445 --> 01:39:13,495
Murderer!

919
01:39:14,985 --> 01:39:16,935
You filthy infidel!

920
01:39:16,935 --> 01:39:19,495
You killed Gonca!
You deserve to die!

921
01:39:19,495 --> 01:39:21,495
Killer! Murderer!

922
01:39:21,585 --> 01:39:24,615
Killer! Murderer! Kill her!
Infidel!

923
01:39:24,615 --> 01:39:30,635
You deserve to die, you killer!
Killer! Murderer!

924
01:39:31,265 --> 01:39:33,485
I will kill all of you!

925
01:39:35,025 --> 01:39:36,925
Filthy Turks!

926
01:39:36,925 --> 01:39:40,765
Killer! Murderer!
Kill her!

927
01:39:42,685 --> 01:39:48,565
-Murderer! Traitor!
-You will die!

928
01:39:48,565 --> 01:39:50,565
You deserve it!

929
01:39:51,115 --> 01:39:55,975
Murderer! Murderer!
Die!

930
01:39:55,975 --> 01:40:04,005
Murderer! Murderer!
You deserve to die! Killer!

931
01:40:04,005 --> 01:40:06,135
Die!

932
01:40:12,425 --> 01:40:14,435
Murderer!

933
01:40:14,435 --> 01:40:15,775
Get up!

934
01:40:29,455 --> 01:40:34,875
Murderer! You will die!
You deserve to die!

935
01:40:36,085 --> 01:40:37,755
You will be punished, Julia!

936
01:40:37,875 --> 01:40:41,455
The mothers of the people you killed
without blinking deserve vengeance!

937
01:40:45,095 --> 01:40:50,095
Now you will pay for Gonca and
my mother.

938
01:40:54,125 --> 01:40:56,825
You separated those innocent children from
their mothers.

939
01:40:56,825 --> 01:41:00,255
You tortured them in many ways. Did you
think you could get away with it?

940
01:41:00,255 --> 01:41:02,025
I am going to kill you!

941
01:41:02,705 --> 01:41:04,025
Shut up!

942
01:41:23,105 --> 01:41:24,845
What is going on here, Malhun Hatun?

943
01:41:25,815 --> 01:41:30,245
While you sit on your throne, we catch
traitors, Gündüz Bey!

944
01:41:35,055 --> 01:41:36,285
Good job.

945
01:41:37,135 --> 01:41:39,065
This devil lived longer than necessary.

946
01:41:41,495 --> 01:41:42,605
How did you do it?

947
01:41:43,125 --> 01:41:45,595
Osman Bey, the Bey of Kayı, ordered.

948
01:41:48,775 --> 01:41:52,475
My Bey is still watching us even when he
is not here.

949
01:41:54,225 --> 01:41:57,645
He predicts all kinds of trouble
and takes precautions

950
01:41:57,795 --> 01:42:01,845
Even like this, Osman Bey took our
revenge.

951
01:42:01,845 --> 01:42:06,605
Osman Bey! Osman Bey! Osman Bey!
Osman Bey! Osman Bey! Osman Bey!

952
01:42:07,040 --> 01:42:20,040
Long live Osman Bey! Long live Osman Bey!
Long live Osman Bey! Long live Osman Bey!

953
01:42:20,175 --> 01:42:22,225
Thank you, Hatuns!

954
01:42:22,675 --> 01:42:24,525
Praise be!

955
01:42:33,895 --> 01:42:37,675
I would leave you to these mothers but...

956
01:42:41,795 --> 01:42:43,335
Alps!

957
01:42:44,835 --> 01:42:46,925
Take her to the lattice tent!

958
01:43:06,875 --> 01:43:09,045
Inegöl Castle

959
01:43:12,335 --> 01:43:13,915
Rogatus!

960
01:43:15,325 --> 01:43:17,775
I guess Osman's plan worked.

961
01:43:18,475 --> 01:43:20,345
You look like you won.

962
01:43:20,925 --> 01:43:24,995
We must include Turks and Mongols
in our armies.

963
01:43:25,545 --> 01:43:27,315
They come in handy when needed.

964
01:43:28,375 --> 01:43:31,565
We won, Nikola.
Osman Bey was right.

965
01:43:32,015 --> 01:43:36,115
You don't need fire to attack
the tribes.

966
01:43:36,115 --> 01:43:40,555
You need it only if you want to attack
the Lord Castles.

967
01:43:41,015 --> 01:43:44,185
They were going to break our walls
with fire, is that so?

968
01:43:45,375 --> 01:43:48,365
Now I am definitely sure that I am on
the right side.

969
01:43:48,915 --> 01:43:50,485
Where is the fire?

970
01:43:50,485 --> 01:43:51,875
Osman has it.

971
01:43:51,885 --> 01:43:53,955
What do you say, Rogatus?

972
01:43:53,955 --> 01:43:55,535
Is this a lesser threat?

973
01:43:55,535 --> 01:43:57,055
Calm down, Nikola.

974
01:43:57,515 --> 01:44:00,125
You are now sure that you are on
the right side.

975
01:44:03,025 --> 01:44:08,085
Emperor Andronikos ordered us to support
Osman.

976
01:44:11,765 --> 01:44:14,185
I will go to Geyhatu and convince him...

977
01:44:14,785 --> 01:44:17,825
...that I am still on his side.

978
01:44:18,975 --> 01:44:21,685
The game must continue.

979
01:44:28,265 --> 01:44:30,415
Praise be!
My valiants!

980
01:44:30,735 --> 01:44:33,275
You destroyed those dogs!

981
01:44:34,025 --> 01:44:36,215
We didn't leave a single one alive,
my Bey.

982
01:44:36,445 --> 01:44:39,465
Great! Thank you.

983
01:44:40,215 --> 01:44:43,185
Kosses, thank you too.

984
01:44:44,675 --> 01:44:46,465
You also helped.

985
01:44:47,225 --> 01:44:48,465
Thank you, Osman Bey.

986
01:44:49,955 --> 01:44:52,705
Fighting for our loved ones with you...

987
01:44:52,705 --> 01:44:53,965
...is an honor.

988
01:44:55,075 --> 01:44:57,245
But to be honest...

989
01:44:57,935 --> 01:45:00,925
...actually Konur saved us from this tough
situation.

990
01:45:01,225 --> 01:45:03,385
Thank you.
Thank you.

991
01:45:04,855 --> 01:45:07,575
What about the fire?
Did you bring it?

992
01:45:07,705 --> 01:45:11,265
Of course, we did, my Bey.
It is with Master Davut.

993
01:45:12,475 --> 01:45:18,025
So, Geyhatu wanted to take the castles
this way.

994
01:45:20,885 --> 01:45:23,525
Yes, my Bey.
I heard those cannibals talking.

995
01:45:23,955 --> 01:45:26,145
They were going to break the walls
with it.

996
01:45:27,985 --> 01:45:33,065
Geyhatu, you will grumble in the gizzard.

997
01:45:33,955 --> 01:45:37,535
I will burn you with that fire.

998
01:46:17,165 --> 01:46:18,685
Look who is here?

999
01:46:20,385 --> 01:46:21,745
Bala!

1000
01:46:26,465 --> 01:46:28,945
And the old woman!

1001
01:46:29,545 --> 01:46:31,315
Why didn't you die!

1002
01:46:36,405 --> 01:46:42,615
I will kill all of you one by one when
I get out of here!

1003
01:46:46,725 --> 01:46:48,285
You vile dog!

1004
01:46:48,745 --> 01:46:50,755
You can't hurt anyone any more!

1005
01:46:51,335 --> 01:46:54,835
You killed my Gonca, killed the alps!

1006
01:46:54,835 --> 01:46:56,845
You even tried to kill children!

1007
01:46:58,115 --> 01:47:01,225
I should've killed the children
right away!

1008
01:47:02,235 --> 01:47:06,745
We would have gotten rid of
a few filthy little Turks.

1009
01:47:12,315 --> 01:47:16,875
Oh, my girl. Who raised you like this,
without love.

1010
01:47:17,395 --> 01:47:21,455
You are talking about killing innocent
children.

1011
01:47:21,875 --> 01:47:24,425
I pity you, my girl.
I pity you.

1012
01:47:25,515 --> 01:47:27,165
Shut up, old woman!

1013
01:47:27,825 --> 01:47:29,695
Why are you still alive?

1014
01:47:30,885 --> 01:47:33,895
Shut up!
Snake!

1015
01:47:39,045 --> 01:47:43,025
You are right, I should've died.

1016
01:47:44,135 --> 01:47:48,205
But I survived with the love of my
children.

1017
01:47:49,175 --> 01:47:51,645
I am here because of their prayers.

1018
01:47:54,005 --> 01:47:55,585
You can't understand this.

1019
01:47:56,665 --> 01:47:58,445
You were never loved.

1020
01:47:59,045 --> 01:48:01,655
You always lived with hatred and grudge.

1021
01:48:02,825 --> 01:48:04,825
But you weren't born like this.

1022
01:48:05,705 --> 01:48:06,825
Oh, my girl.

1023
01:48:07,405 --> 01:48:11,875
One has both good and evil within
herself.

1024
01:48:12,255 --> 01:48:14,615
You always fed the evil side of yours.

1025
01:48:14,975 --> 01:48:17,165
Your goodness faded away.

1026
01:48:17,505 --> 01:48:24,365
Your beauty, your youth...
All turned into a desert.

1027
01:48:25,575 --> 01:48:28,865
You don't know anything, old woman!
Shut up!

1028
01:48:31,625 --> 01:48:34,425
I am going to kill you!

1029
01:48:34,935 --> 01:48:37,445
Then you!

1030
01:48:38,505 --> 01:48:41,535
Then that monster in your belly!

1031
01:48:43,045 --> 01:48:44,385
You!

1032
01:48:45,565 --> 01:48:49,105
Bala, enough.
Come on, my girl.

1033
01:48:52,665 --> 01:48:54,715
You will die first, you devil!

1034
01:48:59,225 --> 01:49:01,025
You'll die!

1035
01:49:09,755 --> 01:49:12,045
We will all die one day.

1036
01:49:12,395 --> 01:49:14,625
We're not afraid of death.

1037
01:49:16,255 --> 01:49:18,755
However, you better start praying.

1038
01:49:19,825 --> 01:49:24,855
Pray, so that Allah accepts it.

1039
01:49:32,485 --> 01:49:36,975
You will die!
I'll kill you all!

1040
01:49:38,165 --> 01:49:39,685
Come here!

1041
01:49:39,735 --> 01:49:41,575
I'll kill you all!

1042
01:49:41,675 --> 01:49:44,935
Bala! Come here!

1043
01:50:04,455 --> 01:50:08,325
Gündüz Bey sent this for the Ahis.

1044
01:50:09,525 --> 01:50:13,045
The Ahis took it from those who
were in heedlessness...

1045
01:50:13,865 --> 01:50:16,725
and gave it to those who are
on the right path.

1046
01:50:17,675 --> 01:50:19,025
We...

1047
01:50:21,395 --> 01:50:25,965
said that it is the right of our Osman
Bey, so we brought it to you.

1048
01:50:27,325 --> 01:50:28,575
Thank you, my Sheikh.

1049
01:50:30,265 --> 01:50:31,835
Thank you.

1050
01:50:32,815 --> 01:50:34,645
Thank Ahis for me.

1051
01:50:35,005 --> 01:50:37,545
These difficult days will pass.

1052
01:50:37,845 --> 01:50:41,395
Your valiants are increasing
from day to day.

1053
01:50:42,105 --> 01:50:45,105
However, the state is a bird.

1054
01:50:45,825 --> 01:50:49,415
It needs two wings, Osman Bey.

1055
01:50:51,365 --> 01:50:54,565
You have many valiants, you
have many men.

1056
01:50:56,825 --> 01:51:01,495
What about scholars?

1057
01:51:03,775 --> 01:51:06,145
Even in this situation, my Sheikh?

1058
01:51:07,745 --> 01:51:12,705
Osman Bey, you live in a shepherd's tent.

1059
01:51:13,835 --> 01:51:17,205
You don't give up on the state.

1060
01:51:18,565 --> 01:51:23,675
Master Davud works actively
with the blacksmiths.

1061
01:51:24,725 --> 01:51:28,215
So many heroes support him.

1062
01:51:30,635 --> 01:51:34,495
He who waits for his time
is always late, Osman Bey.

1063
01:51:36,925 --> 01:51:39,325
The time is now.

1064
01:51:42,375 --> 01:51:43,915
You are right, my Sheikh.

1065
01:51:45,955 --> 01:51:47,305
What would you
like to do?

1066
01:51:47,915 --> 01:51:53,215
With your permission, I would like to
send messengers to all lands.

1067
01:51:54,315 --> 01:52:00,365
I also want the doctrinal foundations for
the blessed state that you will establish.

1068
01:52:02,595 --> 01:52:07,765
And may the bottom of your
flag be filled with scholars.

1069
01:52:10,835 --> 01:52:15,995
My son-in-law, Dursun Fakih, is on the
road with my daughter.

1070
01:52:16,835 --> 01:52:18,665
That's so good, my Sheikh.

1071
01:52:19,095 --> 01:52:22,695
Which permission? They are welcomed.

1072
01:52:22,945 --> 01:52:24,375
Let us host them.

1073
01:52:25,225 --> 01:52:27,495
They always have a place in our hearts.

1074
01:52:37,185 --> 01:52:38,685
Tell me, Osman Bey.

1075
01:52:40,265 --> 01:52:43,505
What is on your mind?

1076
01:52:46,705 --> 01:52:48,085
My Sheikh.

1077
01:52:51,315 --> 01:52:53,035
I need your permission.

1078
01:52:56,325 --> 01:52:57,675
My brother...

1079
01:52:59,595 --> 01:53:01,405
stabbed me in the back.

1080
01:53:04,485 --> 01:53:06,805
He deceived many Turkmens.

1081
01:53:09,685 --> 01:53:11,025
My Sheikh.

1082
01:53:13,025 --> 01:53:18,665
Is my brother's blood halal for me?

1083
01:53:27,145 --> 01:53:28,485
Wait.

1084
01:53:30,385 --> 01:53:32,175
Wait for me, Bala.

1085
01:53:32,965 --> 01:53:34,335
Open the door, brother.

1086
01:53:43,055 --> 01:53:44,415
Boran.

1087
01:53:49,415 --> 01:53:51,485
You will die first.

1088
01:54:10,435 --> 01:54:12,485
You don't talk.

1089
01:54:15,085 --> 01:54:17,585
Have you lost your toxic tongue?

1090
01:54:18,135 --> 01:54:19,715
Mad Boran.

1091
01:54:22,305 --> 01:54:24,385
I wasn't waiting for you.

1092
01:54:26,915 --> 01:54:32,505
You loved your wife like crazy, right?

1093
01:54:34,535 --> 01:54:36,275
Shut up, demon.

1094
01:54:44,265 --> 01:54:45,785
I'll kill you.

1095
01:54:48,385 --> 01:54:49,735
With this?

1096
01:54:54,165 --> 01:54:55,535
Nice.

1097
01:54:56,285 --> 01:54:58,025
That would be easy.

1098
01:54:59,785 --> 01:55:01,335
However, your wife...

1099
01:55:03,135 --> 01:55:07,225
Do you know how she died?
I told you that, right?

1100
01:55:07,525 --> 01:55:08,895
Shut up.

1101
01:55:12,015 --> 01:55:16,545
She was fighting for her life.

1102
01:55:16,995 --> 01:55:18,315
Shut up.

1103
01:55:22,065 --> 01:55:24,565
I am satisfied with you, Boran.

1104
01:55:25,245 --> 01:55:30,035
Do not destroy yourself, please.

1105
01:55:30,975 --> 01:55:32,675
This is not the last time.

1106
01:55:33,725 --> 01:55:35,885
We must meet at the place of gathering.

1107
01:55:35,955 --> 01:55:38,655
Her vessels were torn.

1108
01:55:38,785 --> 01:55:40,785
Shut up, shut up.

1109
01:55:42,235 --> 01:55:44,495
But don't worry, mad Boran.

1110
01:55:46,765 --> 01:55:51,235
I will also send you
where your wife is.

1111
01:56:04,415 --> 01:56:08,525
Come on, come on, do your work, mad Boran.

1112
01:56:10,045 --> 01:56:12,695
Did you think that would be easy?

1113
01:56:13,205 --> 01:56:14,905
Demon.

1114
01:56:15,115 --> 01:56:19,185
What have I told you?
What have I told you?

1115
01:56:21,155 --> 01:56:24,745
I said I won't die before I
make you live the pain...

1116
01:56:24,745 --> 01:56:30,775
you made Gonja live through twice as much.

1117
01:56:34,875 --> 01:56:36,425
I...

1118
01:56:38,425 --> 01:56:40,495
No, no.

1119
01:56:40,935 --> 01:56:42,375
No.

1120
01:56:42,465 --> 01:56:45,255
You will be out of breath first.

1121
01:56:46,585 --> 01:56:49,655
No!

1122
01:56:49,715 --> 01:56:52,815
Your throat will burn with a flame.

1123
01:56:54,115 --> 01:56:59,335
Your vessels will burn one by one as if
they were in the middle of a fire.

1124
01:57:00,115 --> 01:57:04,685
Your body will burn from the
inside and turn to ashes.

1125
01:57:04,835 --> 01:57:07,335
No!

1126
01:57:08,165 --> 01:57:09,465
No!

1127
01:57:09,525 --> 01:57:11,525
For my Gonca!

1128
01:57:54,725 --> 01:57:56,805
Sleep well, my Gonca.

1129
01:57:59,335 --> 01:58:01,045
Sleep well.

1130
01:58:26,495 --> 01:58:28,825
Why were you so surprised
when you saw me?

1131
01:58:35,695 --> 01:58:39,455
You heard that Osman attacked me
on the Nicaea Road, right?

1132
01:58:39,605 --> 01:58:42,445
Geyhatu, I am grateful to you.

1133
01:58:44,755 --> 01:58:46,855
I survived thanks to your soldiers.

1134
01:58:49,275 --> 01:58:51,985
Speak clearly, Nikola.

1135
01:58:52,915 --> 01:58:56,915
The life of a person who speaks
clearly is long.

1136
01:59:00,005 --> 01:59:04,455
When Osman heard that I united with you...

1137
01:59:04,645 --> 01:59:06,825
he tried to harm me.

1138
01:59:07,555 --> 01:59:10,865
Although he had dozens of
reasons to kill me.

1139
01:59:10,935 --> 01:59:12,275
Whatever.

1140
01:59:12,345 --> 01:59:15,175
Your soldiers started attacking
when they saw Osman.

1141
01:59:15,465 --> 01:59:17,535
And I continued on my way, Geyhatu.

1142
01:59:17,775 --> 01:59:21,585
What were you doing in Iznik?

1143
01:59:23,485 --> 01:59:27,075
I talked about the idea of ​​becoming a
state, which you proposed to me...

1144
01:59:27,535 --> 01:59:30,325
with Emperor Andronikos.

1145
01:59:30,705 --> 01:59:32,055
What?

1146
01:59:32,705 --> 01:59:34,035
What did you do?

1147
01:59:39,095 --> 01:59:43,675
Master, hide the Greek fire.

1148
01:59:44,885 --> 01:59:47,595
I will blow them up
to the side of Geyhatu.

1149
01:59:48,095 --> 01:59:51,645
My Bey, people live to die.

1150
01:59:52,255 --> 01:59:55,035
Inshallah I will also see those conquests.

1151
01:59:55,775 --> 01:59:59,305
Master Davud, you are a Master.

1152
01:59:59,655 --> 02:00:01,205
You will be by my side.

1153
02:00:01,395 --> 02:00:04,205
We'll shoot those
castles with your shells.

1154
02:00:04,505 --> 02:00:05,875
However...

1155
02:00:07,435 --> 02:00:09,205
do you know who will throw them?

1156
02:00:12,325 --> 02:00:13,705
You should meet him.

1157
02:00:14,875 --> 02:00:16,405
Shepherd brother.

1158
02:00:17,645 --> 02:00:19,685
You can call me Akça, Master
Davud.

1159
02:00:23,215 --> 02:00:26,605
- Can I come in, my Bey?
- Come in.

1160
02:00:29,455 --> 02:00:32,155
- Salam Alaikum.
- Alaikum Salam.

1161
02:00:34,395 --> 02:00:35,705
Boran.

1162
02:00:36,195 --> 02:00:38,125
Your face is shining, my brother.

1163
02:00:38,295 --> 02:00:41,975
My Bey, I sent that demon to hell.

1164
02:00:42,975 --> 02:00:45,095
I killed Julia, my Bey.

1165
02:00:53,075 --> 02:00:54,795
Today is my feast.

1166
02:00:54,905 --> 02:00:58,645
From now on, the breath I breathe
won't hurt me, my Bey.

1167
02:00:59,125 --> 02:01:00,845
From now on...

1168
02:01:02,175 --> 02:01:03,695
my Bey...

1169
02:01:11,975 --> 02:01:15,975
Brother, this is the end of all cruels.

1170
02:01:16,535 --> 02:01:20,705
Thank Allah I saw you like that.

1171
02:01:20,945 --> 02:01:23,515
Amin, my Bey.

1172
02:01:27,925 --> 02:01:29,275
My Bey.

1173
02:01:30,125 --> 02:01:34,025
Güngüz Bey is going to see Geyhatu.

1174
02:01:45,775 --> 02:01:48,185
Let's go and see Gündüz Bey.

1175
02:01:52,195 --> 02:01:55,625
Let's see if he is still with the cruels.

1176
02:01:57,055 --> 02:01:58,375
Or...

1177
02:02:00,095 --> 02:02:03,145
Or is there a little mercy in his heart?

1178
02:02:08,695 --> 02:02:13,895
If he is still one of the cruels, I'm
sorry for him.

1179
02:02:19,065 --> 02:02:20,615
Let's go.

1180
02:02:24,045 --> 02:02:27,345
Why are you so nervous, Vizier Alemşah?

1181
02:02:29,045 --> 02:02:31,545
I'm still with you.

1182
02:02:33,895 --> 02:02:38,675
I should have taken the emperor's
approval, that's just the matter.

1183
02:02:39,705 --> 02:02:41,085
Why?

1184
02:02:44,225 --> 02:02:45,575
Why?

1185
02:02:46,395 --> 02:02:50,205
So that the emperor won't send an army to
attack me...

1186
02:02:50,220 --> 02:02:54,010
when you leave these lands, Geyhatu.

1187
02:02:58,245 --> 02:03:04,195
You went to see the emperor and told
him that you will establish a state...

1188
02:03:05,165 --> 02:03:08,595
and you got out
safely, didn't you, Nikola?

1189
02:03:09,865 --> 02:03:11,145
Yes.

1190
02:03:13,995 --> 02:03:16,095
This is exactly what happened.

1191
02:03:16,725 --> 02:03:19,975
The emperor is very afraid of Geyhatu.

1192
02:03:20,345 --> 02:03:25,245
If Geyhatu says that Nikola
will be the emperor.

1193
02:03:27,545 --> 02:03:30,355
The Emperor Andronikos will not
think for a moment...

1194
02:03:30,375 --> 02:03:33,845
and he will leave his throne and his
crown and give me Constantinople.

1195
02:03:33,885 --> 02:03:39,125
He told me, "Don't piss them off and do
whatever they want."

1196
02:03:39,225 --> 02:03:46,795
If there's something bad in this, I'll rip
your heart out and feed it to the dogs.

1197
02:03:47,425 --> 02:03:50,875
No trick, Geyhatu.

1198
02:03:51,345 --> 02:03:53,475
Emperor Andronikos.

1199
02:03:53,795 --> 02:03:59,175
He wants us to put the Turks among
us and crush them like flies.

1200
02:04:02,375 --> 02:04:06,995
Roma is with you, great Geyhatu.

1201
02:04:26,525 --> 02:04:30,925
Help Geyhatu to stop the Turks.

1202
02:04:31,225 --> 02:04:32,725
The Emperor.

1203
02:04:41,375 --> 02:04:42,695
Good.

1204
02:04:43,295 --> 02:04:45,995
Go now, Gündüz will come.

1205
02:04:46,195 --> 02:04:47,575
He shouldn't see you.

1206
02:04:51,025 --> 02:04:53,075
Whatever you want.

1207
02:05:29,485 --> 02:05:31,585
Stupid Nikola.

1208
02:05:32,785 --> 02:05:35,355
I don't know what he's up to.

1209
02:05:37,785 --> 02:05:42,955
But I'll take Inegol from him.

1210
02:05:44,955 --> 02:05:50,435
Even if there was a trick, he wouldn't
live enough to complete it.

1211
02:05:50,885 --> 02:05:54,585
We will enter his castle amicably.

1212
02:05:56,585 --> 02:06:00,085
And we'll take it out from under him.

1213
02:06:00,735 --> 02:06:04,705
Nikola hasn't learned to
sit on his castle.

1214
02:06:05,085 --> 02:06:12,105
When the Greek fire comes, and then no
one will be able to stand in our way.

1215
02:06:19,535 --> 02:06:20,955
Speak.

1216
02:06:25,005 --> 02:06:27,435
The soldiers sent by Argun Khan...

1217
02:06:29,185 --> 02:06:31,685
and the unit was destroyed.

1218
02:06:36,585 --> 02:06:38,155
The Greek fire...

1219
02:06:40,555 --> 02:06:42,055
is unavailable.

1220
02:06:46,295 --> 02:06:49,355
You didn't even tell me about the route.

1221
02:06:54,305 --> 02:06:58,355
How and who got the news, Geyhatu?

1222
02:07:02,215 --> 02:07:04,215
Osman.

1223
02:07:32,605 --> 02:07:36,205
- Gündüz Bey.
- Osman Bey.

1224
02:07:37,285 --> 02:07:39,005
Come here.

1225
02:07:41,765 --> 02:07:44,615
Come here, Gündüz Bey.

1226
02:07:48,475 --> 02:07:54,035
I don't want the blood of my brothers
and Alps to be shed.

1227
02:08:13,875 --> 02:08:16,185
You want to hurt Turks with the cruels...

1228
02:08:17,485 --> 02:08:20,325
with the support of the Alps.

1229
02:08:23,535 --> 02:08:25,585
They are not to blame.

1230
02:08:26,155 --> 02:08:27,605
You...

1231
02:08:28,395 --> 02:08:33,005
were deceived by the Vizier and Geyhatu
and you deceive them.

1232
02:08:50,535 --> 02:08:52,205
All my life...

1233
02:08:53,755 --> 02:08:57,895
I witnessed what your sword
did to the cruel people.

1234
02:09:01,405 --> 02:09:03,855
Since you are one of the cruels now...

1235
02:09:05,585 --> 02:09:07,185
then...

1236
02:09:13,205 --> 02:09:16,085
meet my sword of my justice.

1237
02:09:20,235 --> 02:09:22,305
Come on, Gündüz Bey.

1238
02:09:26,475 --> 02:09:30,255
Since you consider me as an enemy...

1239
02:09:33,495 --> 02:09:37,085
Then I won't back down, brother.

1240
02:09:38,705 --> 02:09:41,835
After all the betrayals you've done...

1241
02:09:42,665 --> 02:09:46,735
after all the cruelty,do you still call
me my brother?

1242
02:09:49,585 --> 02:09:51,285
Wha brother?

1243
02:09:53,905 --> 02:09:58,065
From now on, I'm not your brother.

1244
02:09:58,885 --> 02:10:01,035
I don't give up on my brother.

1245
02:10:10,215 --> 02:10:12,855
Because of the betrayals you've made...

1246
02:10:15,205 --> 02:10:18,385
your blood is halal.

1247
02:10:22,705 --> 02:10:27,355
You betrayed your ancestral inheritance.

1248
02:10:28,155 --> 02:10:32,605
You are a brother who left his
brother among traitors.

1249
02:10:34,255 --> 02:10:39,235
You are a Bey who has turned
his back on his state.

1250
02:10:45,035 --> 02:10:46,755
You will leave this world now...

1251
02:10:48,585 --> 02:10:50,285
without a brother...

1252
02:10:51,555 --> 02:10:53,385
nor customs...

1253
02:10:54,105 --> 02:10:56,555
nor a homeland.

1254
02:11:02,035 --> 02:11:03,385
Come here.

1255
02:11:55,635 --> 02:11:57,305
Come on.

1256
02:12:00,985 --> 02:12:02,685
Come on, brother.

1257
02:12:04,885 --> 02:12:07,055
After all the betrayals...

1258
02:12:08,535 --> 02:12:10,805
After all the cruelty...

1259
02:12:11,895 --> 02:12:14,255
you will be a brother killer.

1260
02:12:15,005 --> 02:12:16,505
Come on.

1261
02:12:18,735 --> 02:12:21,835
Your instinct is like the instinct of Cain.

1262
02:12:22,955 --> 02:12:25,005
I didn't want to be Cain...

1263
02:12:27,005 --> 02:12:28,585
nor to be a traitor.

1264
02:12:30,305 --> 02:12:32,335
The sword of justice...

1265
02:12:38,245 --> 02:12:39,955
can...

1266
02:12:40,855 --> 02:12:42,405
take my soul.

1267
02:12:56,955 --> 02:12:58,505
Alps!

1268
02:12:59,425 --> 02:13:01,055
You should know...

1269
02:13:01,955 --> 02:13:03,285
what I did was...

1270
02:13:05,005 --> 02:13:08,585
not because of my greed, nor because
of my love for the position.

1271
02:13:08,855 --> 02:13:13,015
Remember me as someone who veered
out of his way...

1272
02:13:13,325 --> 02:13:19,725
thinking about the safety of the Kayı.

1273
02:13:25,435 --> 02:13:27,435
The time has come, my brother.

1274
02:13:29,605 --> 02:13:31,455
Our ways are separated.

1275
02:13:33,455 --> 02:13:35,455
You are on the right path...

1276
02:13:37,285 --> 02:13:40,455
and I am the one who blinded his eyes by
the curtain of omission.

1277
02:13:41,225 --> 02:13:42,935
I made a mistake.

1278
02:13:43,785 --> 02:13:45,505
I was oblivious.

1279
02:13:46,385 --> 02:13:48,935
From now on, my blood is halal
for you, my brother.

1280
02:13:52,485 --> 02:13:54,035
Come on, brother

1281
02:13:55,725 --> 02:13:57,255
Come on.

1282
02:14:40,155 --> 02:14:42,955
Our ways were the same.

1283
02:14:47,085 --> 02:14:49,735
However, you couldn't walk.

1284
02:14:57,865 --> 02:15:00,585
Our goal was the same.

1285
02:15:02,115 --> 02:15:04,635
You didn't keep it.

1286
02:15:14,805 --> 02:15:17,755
I was behind you like a mountain.

1287
02:15:19,755 --> 02:15:22,755
However, you didn't stand upright.

1288
02:15:42,385 --> 02:15:45,165
The cost is now known.

1289
02:15:58,005 --> 02:16:00,605
Who does not stand by his words...

1290
02:16:02,285 --> 02:16:04,305
ends up like this.

1291
02:17:02,285 --> 02:17:21,174
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com